{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jkcnv72fH4fX94u7EHdzRS","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (67.4KB). Full output saved to: /home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/8e4fb739-e3b4-441f-9ea8-cd85c9144370/tool-results/bsn4ifwbx.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n# Web coverage atlas\n\nLane: a LIVE challenge-owned target per question (`targets[{id:\"Target N\", url}]`, no artifact), one `proof-N`\nquestion per target, answer = the token `proof_<32 hex>` the app prints once the bug is exploited (`trim`). One\nclassic bug per lane-day, named by a title pun: D01 exposed backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi, D04 path traversal, D05\nunprotected feature route, D06 reflected XSS (server-judged callback), D07 stored XSS (real moderator bot), D08\nsession fixation, D09 CSRF (judged by `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`), D10 upload rendered by a `{{field}}` preview,\nD11 SSTI, D12 second-order SQLi, D13 mass assignment, D14 per-field/action API authz, D15 SSRF to 127.0.0.1:8080,\nD16 OS command injection, D17 password reset token not bound to its account, D18 GraphQL resolver without\nfield-level authz, D19 unauthenticated webhook trusting forged events (\"Trust the Webhook\": one JSON body with the\nclue `event_type`/`owner_scope` values under every alias + role/source/trust flags), D20 unsigned client-side state\nblob (\"Serialized Offender\": `{\"state\": b64url('{\"user\":..,\"role\":\"administrator\"}')}`), D21 race / double spend\n(\"Double Spent\": one credit, burst concurrent POSTs; UNSOLVED, the target was burned before the burst), D22 WebSocket\nevent stream without authz (\"Socket to Me\": handshake + `Origin` + `?stream=<stream_reference>`), D23 trusted\nreverse-proxy header (\"Forwarded Misgivings\": `X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1` past `loopback_only`). Since D05 every target is\nthe same kit: `/api/clues` names `feature_route`, often `secondary_route`, `current_role: analyst` (D18\n`current_user`) + usually one concept key (`callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`/`receipt_route_template`,\n`session_hint`, `preferences_route`, `preview_guide`/`upload_policy`/`upload_shape`, `inventory_route`/\n`protected_reference`, `input_parameter`/`example_path`, `recovery_guide_route`, `protected_reference`+`note`,\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8e4fb739-e3b4-441f-9ea8-cd85c9144370","uuid":"63a68ce2-3110-408f-83c5-ddca47044fc8","timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:07:35.188Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Web coverage atlas\n\nLane: a LIVE challenge-owned target per question (`targets[{id:\"Target N\", url}]`, no artifact), one `proof-N`\nquestion per target, answer = the token `proof_<32 hex>` the app prints once the bug is exploited (`trim`). One\nclassic bug per lane-day, named by a title pun: D01 exposed backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi, D04 path traversal, D05\nunprotected feature route, D06 reflected XSS (server-judged callback), D07 stored XSS (real moderator bot), D08\nsession fixation, D09 CSRF (judged by `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`), D10 upload rendered by a `{{field}}` preview,\nD11 SSTI, D12 second-order SQLi, D13 mass assignment, D14 per-field/action API authz, D15 SSRF to 127.0.0.1:8080,\nD16 OS command injection, D17 password reset token not bound to its account, D18 GraphQL resolver without\nfield-level authz, D19 unauthenticated webhook trusting forged events (\"Trust the Webhook\": one JSON body with the\nclue `event_type`/`owner_scope` values under every alias + role/source/trust flags), D20 unsigned client-side state\nblob (\"Serialized Offender\": `{\"state\": b64url('{\"user\":..,\"role\":\"administrator\"}')}`), D21 race / double spend\n(\"Double Spent\": one credit, burst concurrent POSTs; UNSOLVED, the target was burned before the burst), D22 WebSocket\nevent stream without authz (\"Socket to Me\": handshake + `Origin` + `?stream=<stream_reference>`), D23 trusted\nreverse-proxy header (\"Forwarded Misgivings\": `X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1` past `loopback_only`). Since D05 every target is\nthe same kit: `/api/clues` names `feature_route`, often `secondary_route`, `current_role: analyst` (D18\n`current_user`) + usually one concept key (`callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`/`receipt_route_template`,\n`session_hint`, `preferences_route`, `preview_guide`/`upload_policy`/`upload_shape`, `inventory_route`/\n`protected_reference`, `input_parameter`/`example_path`, `recovery_guide_route`, `protected_reference`+`note`,\n`event_type`+`owner_scope` (body values), `state_format_route`, `stream_reference` (int value), `deployment:\ntrusted_reverse_proxy` (value)). D11-D13, D15 and D21 had NO concept key: the prompt and\nthe bare-route errors were the routing signal. Stated policies and echoes are costume. Success = proof regex, never\n`effect` alone (D12 empty rows; D16's harmless baseline already says `worker_command_completed`). Any file read shows\n`/run/huntress/config.json` whose `weakness` names the class. Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days (4 targets\nsince D15, 5 on cal. 27), described only by today's prompt -> earlier-day solvers must not read params from it.\nPace: D01-D03 cal. 19, D04-D05 cal. 20, D06-D08 cal. 21, D09-D10 cal. 22, D11-D13 cal. 23, D14-D15 cal. 24, D16-D18\ncal. 25, D19-D20 cal. 26, D21-D23 cal. 27 -> D24-D31 (8 lane-days) over cal. 28-31, ~2 per day; priority 1 below =\nlikely in D24-D29.\nArc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read -> XSS (reflected, stored) -> session -> CSRF ->\nupload -> SSTI -> second-order SQLi -> OWASP API run (API3/API5 mass assignment + field/action authz, API7 SSRF) ->\nOS command injection -> authentication flow (API2: reset) -> GraphQL -> integrity failures (OWASP A08 / API10: D19\nunsigned webhook, D20 unsigned state) -> infrastructure / protocol trust (D21 race in a one-credit ledger, D22 WS\nupgrade skipping authz, D23 proxy client-IP header). Since D19 every day was a NEW concept, not a