e same prompt dependence.\")\ng[\"codify-before-tt\"][\"detail\"]=(\"REGRESSED AGAIN on cal. 28 (D24 Fail Open Friday): the answer-first worker submitted a by-hand proof 41 s after start, which unlocked TT at once; the plugin day28_web_fail_open_friday.py landed ~28 s after TT start -> TT solver_incomplete (live worker CORRECT ~42 s after TT start). D25 promoted its plugin before submit -> TT first try (solve 5 s). Cal. 27: D22 plugin 20 s late -> TT solver_incomplete; D23 in time -> 10.5 s. Fix: the single submit (by ANY worker, answer-first included) must wait until the class plugin is importable and has returned the same proof on the live target, OR TT start must be gated on it. Earlier: TT solver_incomplete on D09, D10, D12, D13, D15-D18; fixed on D19-D20 by the 45 s grace at CORRECT.\")\ng[\"vcs-debug-leak-reader\"][\"priority\"]=1\ng[\"vcs-debug-leak-reader\"][\"detail\"]=\"Raised to 1 after cal. 28: OWASP 2025 A02 Security Misconfiguration is unseen and a likely D26-D31 day; see also security-misconfig-probe. \"+g[\"vcs-debug-leak-reader\"][\"detail\"]\ng[\"crypto-weak-token-derivation\"][\"priority\"]=1\ng[\"crypto-weak-token-derivation\"][\"detail\"]=\"Raised to 1 after cal. 28: OWASP 2025 A04 Cryptographic Failures is unseen while D24/D25 took A10/A09 -- pair with jwt-session-forge. \"+g[\"crypto-weak-token-derivation\"][\"detail\"]\nfor k in [\"path-verb-normalization-bypass\",\"business-logic-tamper\",\"alias-union-body-builder\",\"dom-xss-sink-scan\",\"open-redirect-planner\",\"prototype-pollution\",\"api-shadow-version\",\"nosql-operator-injection\",\"clue-json-router\",\"mastery-concept-dispatcher\",\"fetch-metadata-matrix\",\"stopgate-503-already-solved\"]:\n    g[k][\"priority\"]=2\ng[\"log-injection-forging\"][\"priority\"]=2\ng[\"log-injection-forging\"][\"detail\"]=\"D25 'If a Breach Falls in a Log' was the A09 'missing event' form (protected_export logged as page_view; report the gap via the audit log's own report schema). Forging/injection is the remaining sibling. \"+g[\"log-injection-forging\"][\"detail\"]\ng[\"mfa-step-skip-auth-flow\"][\"detail\"]=\"A07:2025 Authentication Failures is the only 2025 category touched just once (D17) -- keep priority 1. \"+g[\"mfa-step-skip-auth-flow\"][\"detail\"]\ng[\"jwt-session-forge\"][\"detail\"]=g[\"jwt-session-forge\"][\"detail\"].replace(\"Still unseen after D23\",\"Still unseen after D25 (OWASP 2025 A04/A07 territory, both open)\")\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"owasp2025-remaining-categories\",\"concept\":\"forecast: D24/D25 took OWASP Top 10:2025's A10 and A09; D26-D31 likely cover A02, A03, A04, A07\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"Cal. 28 showed the tail of the lane walking OWASP Top 10:2025: D24 Fail Open Friday = A10 Mishandling of Exceptional Conditions (new in 2025), D25 If a Breach Falls in a Log = A09 Security Logging & Alerting Failures. Earlier days covered A01 (D02, D05, D14, D18), A05 Injection (D03, D11, D12, D16), A06 Insecure Design (D21 race), A08 Integrity (D19, D20). Unseen: A02 Security Misconfiguration (security-misconfig-probe, vcs-debug-leak-reader, cors-misconfig-probe, xxe-payloads), A03 Software Supply Chain Failures (supply-chain-integrity, known-vulnerable-component), A04 Cryptographic Failures (jwt-session-forge, crypto-weak-token-derivation), A07 Authentication Failures (default-creds-login, mfa-step-skip-auth-flow). Workers: when a prompt reads like an OWASP category description, map it to the category first, then to the gap's first move. Recent kits self-document: a *_format_route guide or a `report{method, fields}` schema tells you the exact request.\"},\n {\"id\":\"security-misconfig-probe\",\"concept\":\"security misconfiguration: debug mode, verbose errors, default config, exposed admin/console, directory listing (row 49, OWASP A02:2025)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Unseen 2025 category, likely D26-D31. Kit guess: clue value like `environment: development` / `debug: true` / `config_route`, or a feature that 500s with a stack trace. Pure planner over recon bodies: GET (capped, once each) /debug, /actuator, /actuator/env, /actuator/configprops, /console, /server-status, /server-info, /phpinfo.php, /.env, /config.json, /api/config, /trace, /_profiler, /elmah.axd, /swagger-ui, directory listing on any clue route's parent; force a verbose error (wrong type, missing field, Accept: text/html) on each clue route and parse the 500 body for secrets/keys/hidden routes. Use what it reveals: a debug toggle param (?debug=1, X-Debug: 1), an admin route, a default/dev credential, a signing secret (hand to jwt-session-forge). Parser: proof regex + secret/route extraction. GET only; no scanning beyond this list.\"},\n {\"id\":\"supply-chain-integrity\",\"concept\":\"software supply chain: dependency / plugin / update fetched or installed without integrity verification (row 50, OWASP A03:2025)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Unseen 2025 category, likely D26-D31. Kit guess (same style as D24's guide): a `*_manifest_route` / `package_route` / `registry` / `update_route` clue whose guide documents {source, name, version, integrity/sha256, signature}; the feature installs/loads what you point it at. Planner: replay the documented sample (baseline), then one change at a time: source/registry URL -> an app-owned route (secondary_route, /api/clues) or a higher version of the same name (dependency confusion), integrity/sha256 mismatched / empty / removed / algorithm swapped (sha256 -> md5/none), signature missing, version pinned -> `latest` / `*`, script tag without SRI. Effect JSON + evidence expected. Reuse the D20/D24 format-guide reader. Parser: proof regex.\"},\n {\"id\":\"default-creds-login\",\"concept\":\"default / documented / leaked credentials (row 14, OWASP A07:2025)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"A07 touched only by D17. Planner: collect credential-shaped pairs the app itself shows (HTML comments, JS literals, *_guide/format routes, README/backup files, error messages, 'factory settings'/'setup' pages, the framework's documented defaults table for the CURRENT banner only: admin/admin, admin/password, root/root, guest/guest, tomcat/tomcat, etc. -- at most ~8 tries, no brute force). Login endpoints from forms / clues / openapi; JSON then form body. After login, GET the secondary/admin route. Parser: proof regex; session cookie carried.\"},\n {\"id\":\"format-guide-mutator\",\"concept\":\"generic *_format_route / *_guide_route reader: replay the documented sample, then mutate one field (D20 data tamper, D24 malformed input)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Two days (D20 /api/state-format, D24 /api/policy-format) shipped a JSON guide describing the exact request: {transport | query_parameter | request_field, prefix, encoding ('base64url of UTF-8 JSON' / 'base64url UTF-8 JSON'), sample_state | sample_decision, sample_encoded}. Pure planner: input = guide JSON + clues (incl. any value key such as expected_behavior); output = ordered request list: (1) the sample as documented (baseline; never a solve), (2) DATA mutations (role/scope/allow/admin ladder: administrator, admin, ...; allow true; scope private/internal/admin), (3) FORMAT mutations keeping the prefix: undecodable payload (%%%invalid, !!!), truncated, empty, valid base64 of non-JSON, JSON of wrong type ([], 1, null), missing prefix, unknown prefix/version, oversized. Encoding per guide (b64url no padding). Parser: proof regex. Covers D20/D24 and their sequels with one module.\"},\n {\"id\":\"exceptional-condition-sequels\",\"concept\":\"A10 sequels: other fail-open / error-path flaws (row 48b)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D24 failed open on an undecodable policy. Siblings: upstream timeout / unavailable (a clue naming a remote service URL or timeout parameter -> point it at an unroutable app-owned path), exception in a check skipped by a catch-all (wrong JSON type, missing field, null, huge integer, invalid UTF-8, duplicate key), error responses leaking data (stack traces, SQL, secrets) -> read every 4xx/5xx body for the proof. Planner over each request field the clues/guide name; one mutation per request; GET the protected route after each. Parser: proof regex. Reuse format-guide-mutator.\"},\n]\ngaps=[x for x in gaps]+new\n# order by priority stable\ngaps.sort(key=lambda x:x[\"priority\"])\nassert len({x['id'] for x in gaps})==len(gaps)\nbody=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False) for x in gaps)+\"\\n]\\n\"\ns=s[:i+8]+body+s[j:]\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\npending=[x for x in gaps if x[\"action\"]==\"prebuild\"]\nprint(len(gaps), len(pending), sum(1 for x in pending if x[\"priority\"]==1))\nEOF\npython3 -c \"\nimport json,re;s=open('reference/coverage/web.md').read();i=s.index('\\`\\`\\`json\\n');j=s.index('\\`\\`\\`',i+8);g=json.loads(s[i+8:j]);print('valid',len(g), set(k for x in g for k in x))\"; wc -l reference/coverage/web.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3795,"cache_read_input_tokens":144941,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3795},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8e4fb739-e3b4-441f-9ea8-cd85c9144370","uuid":"c7d678a4-9376-44b6-b441-67e9cef8d26d","timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:13:52.640Z","request_id":"req_011CgUhCSDxopUGKxt3Tdpk6","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017VTg3mm8hAYbEeFXwzTqcq":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np=\"reference/coverage/web.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1, a[:70]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"\"\"?doc= (handbook.php/notes.php), \"stay inside\"          -> traversal          -> ../